\c 1
\ms1 Yehezkel's calling to be a prophet
\mr (1:1–3:27)
\s1 Yahweh reveals himself
\rem /s1 The Living Creatures and the Glory of the Lord; The calling of Ezekiel; A Vision of Living Beings; The Vision of the Chariot; God's Throne
\p
\v 1 \add When¦333469 I was\add* thirty¦333471 years \add old\add*, on¦333471 July 5th, as I was \add ≈living with¦333471 the other captives\add* by the Kebar¦333484 Canal, the skies¦333486 opened¦333485 and¦333469 I saw¦333487 visions¦333488 from God¦333489.\x + \xo 1:1: \xt Rev 19:11.\x*
\p
\v 2 That was the fifth¦333495 year¦333494 since King¦333497 Yoyakin \add (Jehoiachin)\add* had been taken captive.\x + \xo 1:2: \xt 2Ki 24:10-16; 2Ch 36:9-10.\x*
\v 3 Yahweh gave \add me\add*, the priest¦333511 Yehezkel (son of Buzi¦333510), this message¦333502 in the land¦333512 of the Chaldeans \add (often known better as Babylonians)\add* by the Kebar¦333518 Canal, and Yahweh \add ≈revealed his strength to me\add* there¦333521.
\v 4 Then¦333526 I¦333527 looked¦333526, and there was a windstorm coming¦333530 from the north¦333533—a huge¦333535 cloud with \add ≈lightning\add* flashing¦333537 inside it and \add ≈brilliant light\add* inside it and surrounding it, and fire inside the cloud \add ≈made it look\add* amber¦333543 coloured.
\v 5 In the middle¦333547 \add ≈was what seemed to be\add* four¦333549 living¦333550 creatures¦333550 resembling humans¦333554,\x + \xo 1:5: \xt Rev 4:6.\x*
\v 6 \add ≈but¦333557\add* each of them had four faces¦333558 and¦333557 four wings¦333561.
\v 7 Their legs were straight¦333567, but¦333565 they¦333573 had hooves like calves' hooves that gleamed¦333574 like polished bronze¦333575.
\v 8 They had human¦333580 hands¦333578 under¦333581 their wings on each of their four sides¦333585. For each of the four of them,
\v 9 their¦333595 wings were touching¦333590 the wings of the next creature, and they didn't¦333596 turn as they went—rather each one went straight forward.
\p
\v 10 Each one's \add front¦333609\add* face¦333608 was like a human¦333610 face, then¦333607 they each had a lion's face on the right¦333615, a calf's face on the left, and¦333607 the fourth \add face\add* was an eagle's¦333624 face.\x + \xo 1:10: \xt Ezr 1:5,10; 10:4; Eze 10:14; Rev 4:7.\x*
\v 11 Their faces¦333627 were like that, and their wings were spread¦333629 out above¦333630, so that each creature had a pair of wings that touched¦333633 another creature's wings, and also a pair that covered¦333636 their bodies¦333638.
\v 12 Each went straight forward, so that wherever¦333648 the spirit¦333652 directed them to go¦333653, they went without turning.
\p
\v 13 The living creatures \add ≈resembled\add* burning¦333665 coals¦333662 \add ≈or\add* torches¦333667. Bright fire also moved around among the creatures, and¦333659 there were flashes of lightning¦333678.\x + \xo 1:13: \xt Rev 4:5.\x*
\v 14 The living¦333680 creatures¦333680 moved rapidly swiftly back and forth, and they¦333681 \add ≈looked a bit like\add* lightning¦333684.
\p
\v 15 Then¦333686 I¦333688 looked¦333686 \add ≈more closely\add* and¦333686 saw a wheel¦333689 on the ground beside¦333692 each of the living creatures with its four faces¦333695.\x + \xo 1:15-21: \xt Eze 10:9-13.\x*
\v 16 \add ≈Each of the wheels was the same, and they all shone like\add* chrysolite¦333701. \add ≈Each wheel seemed to have one wheel inside another\add* wheel.
\v 17 \add When\add* they moved, \add ≈they didn't¦333719 have to turn to change direction¦333716\add*.
\v 18 The rims \add @of the wheels\add* were \add ≈awesomely¦333726 tall\add*, and¦333723 all four¦333732 of them were full of eyes¦333730 around¦333731 the rim.\x + \xo 1:18: \xt Rev 4:8.\x*
\v 19 Whenever the living creatures moved, the wheels moved beside¦333738 them. When¦333734 the living creatures \add ≈went upwards\add*, the wheels also went up.
\v 20 Wherever the spirit would go, they went, and the wheels went up beside them, because¦333760 the spirit of the living¦333762 creature was in¦333763 the wheels.
\v 21 Whenever the creatures moved, the wheels also moved, and when the creatures stood still, the wheels stood still. When the creatures \add ≈went upwards\add*, the wheels went up beside them, because¦333775 the spirit¦333776 of the living¦333777 creature was in¦333767 the wheels.
\p
\v 22 Above the living¦333784 creatures was \add ≈something like an awesome¦333788 crystal¦333787 dome stretched out over their¦333792 heads\add*.\x + \xo 1:22: \xt Rev 4:6.\x*
\v 23 Beneath the dome, each of the creatures' wings stretched out straight¦333798 and¦333807 touched another creature's wings. Each \add *one\add* also had a pair to cover their¦333797 own body¦333812 with.
\v 24 Then¦333814 I heard¦333814 the sound of their wings, \add which was\add* like the noise of a lot of water¦333820. When¦333814 they moved¦333825, it was like the voice¦333822 of the powerful \add one\add*—like the sound of a rainstorm¦333827 \add or\add* an army. Whenever they stood¦333830 still¦333830, they lowered their wings.\x + \xo 1:24: \xt Rev 1:4-15; 19:6.\x*
\v 25 Whenever they stopped¦333843 and¦333834 lowered their wings¦333845, a voice came from under¦333837 the dome that¦333839 was above¦333840 their heads¦333842.
\s1 God's throne
\p
\v 26 Above the dome over their¦333852 heads¦333852 was \add ≈what looked like a sapphire¦333856 stone¦333854 that had been made into\add* a throne, and¦333847 on the thing like a throne was \add ≈something that looked like\add* a man.\x + \xo 1:26: \xt Eze 10:1; Rev 4:2-3.\x*
\v 27 I saw a figure \add ≈that appeared to have\add* glowing metal with fire in it from his hips upwards¦333881, and \add ≈looking downwards¦333884 from\add* his hips, I saw the appearance of fire and brightness¦333889 all around.\x + \xo 1:27: \xt Eze 8:2.\x*
\v 28 The bright¦333902 light surrounding \add @the throne\add* \add ≈looked like\add* a rainbow¦333894 in¦333897 the clouds¦333897 on¦333897 a rainy¦333899 day¦333898—it was the appearance of the likeness¦333906 of Yahweh's¦333909 splendour¦333907. When I saw¦333910 it¦333896, I \add ≈quickly knelt down and bowed my head to the ground\add*, and I heard¦333915 a voice¦333916 speaking.
\c 2
\s1 Yehezkel sent as a prophet to Yisrael
\rem /s1 Ezekiel's Call and Commission; Ezekiel's Call; The Vision of the Scroll
\p
\v 1 He said¦333920 to me, “Humanity's child, stand¦333925 up and then I'll speak¦333929 to you¦333930.”
\v 2 Then¦333932 as he spoke to me, the spirit¦333934 entered¦333932 into me and \add ≈stood me up\add*, and I¦333942 heard¦333942 him speaking to me.
\v 3 He told me, “Humanity's child, I'm sending¦333953 you¦333955 to Yisrael's people¦333958—\add two\add* rebellious nations¦333962 that¦333964 have rebelled¦333965 against me. Both they and their¦333969 ancestors¦333969 have been sinning against me \add ≈right up to this very moment\add*.
\v 4 Their descendants¦333978 \add ≈are very stubborn¦333981 and hardheaded\add*. I'm sending¦333985 you to them, and you'll tell them that this is what the master¦333992 Yahweh¦333992 is saying to them.
\v 5 They might listen¦333998 or might not. They're a rebellious¦334004 \add ≈bunch\add*, but¦333995 they'll at¦334010 least know¦334006 that a prophet's¦334008 been among¦334010 them.
\p
\v 6 And you, humanity's¦334016 child, don't¦334017 be afraid of them or their words. Don't be afraid, even though you're¦334032 among briers¦334027 and thorns¦334027, and although you live with scorpions¦334031. Don't fear their words or be dismayed¦334041 by their faces¦334038, since they're a rebellious¦334044 \add ≈bunch\add*.
\v 7 \add ≈Pass my\add* messages¦334050 on to them, whether¦334052 they listen¦334054 or not, because¦334058 they're \add quite\add* rebellious¦334059.
\v 8 \add ≈But¦334063\add* you, humanity's¦334066 child, listen¦334067 to what I'm telling you. Don't¦334074 become rebellious like that¦334069 rebellious \add ≈bunch\add*. Open your mouth¦334082 and eat¦334083 what I'm \add about to\add* give you.”
\v 9 Then¦334091 I looked¦334091 and saw¦334091 a hand¦334094 extended out to me, and \add ≈it was holding a scroll¦334100 with writing on it\add*.\x + \xo 2:9-10: \xt Rev 5:1.\x*
\v 10 He spread¦334104 it out \add ≈in front of\add* me—there was writing on both the front and the back, \add ≈and it was full of messages about grief, mourning¦334114, and sad endings\add*.
\c 3
\p
\v 1 He said to me, “Humanity's child, eat what you've found. Eat this scroll¦334131, then go speak¦334134 to the \add ≈Israeli¦334137 people\add*.”\x + \xo 3:1-3: \xt Rev 10:9-10.\x*
\v 2 So¦334140 I opened¦334140 my mouth¦334143, and¦334140 he gave¦334144 me the scroll¦334146 to eat¦334144.
\p
\v 3 He told me, “Humanity's child, feed your belly¦334154 and fill¦334157 your stomach with¦334167 this scroll¦334159 that¦334161 I've given you.” So¦334149 I ate¦334165 it, and it \add ≈tasted\add* as sweet¦334169 as honey¦334168.
\p
\v 4 Then he told me, “Humanity's child, go to the \add ≈people\add* of Yisrael¦334183 \add (Israel¦334183)\add* and \add ≈pass\add* my messages¦334185 on¦334185 to them,
\v 5 because you aren't¦334189 being¦334198 sent to a people group \add ≈who speak\add* a strange or difficult¦334195 language, but¦334195 to the \add ≈Israeli¦334202 people\add*—
\v 6 not to many people¦334208 groups \add ≈who speak\add* strange or difficult¦334212 languages whose words¦334218 you wouldn't be able to understand¦334217. \add ≈I'm sure that if it was them that\add* I sent¦334223 you to, they would've listened¦334225 to you.
\v 7 \add ≈But¦334228\add* the \add ≈Israeli people\add* won't¦334230 be willing to listen to you, because¦334234 they're not willing to listen to me. All the \add ≈Israeli people\add* are \add ≈hardheaded\add* and¦334228 hardhearted.
\v 8 \add ≈Listen, I'll enable you to be as stubborn and¦334261 tough as they are\add*.
\v 9 I'll¦334271 make¦334271 \add ≈you hard\add* like a diamond¦334268—harder than flint¦334270. Don't¦334273 \add ≈be scared¦334279 by\add* them or discouraged¦334279 by \add ≈the looks they give you\add*, because¦334281 they're rebellious¦334284 \add ≈people\add*.”
\p
\v 10 He \add ≈also\add* told me, “Humanity's child, \add ≈listen¦334304 very carefully to what I say\add*, and \add ≈keep thinking about it\add*.
\v 11 Then¦334306 go¦334307 to \add ≈any of your¦334314 people¦334314 who were brought here as\add* captives, and¦334306 tell them, ‘This¦334322 is what the master¦334321 Yahweh¦334321 says¦334320,’ whether¦334323 they'll listen¦334325 or not.”
\rem /s1 Ezekiel at the River Chebar
\p
\v 12 Then¦334330 the spirit¦334331 lifted¦334330 me up, and¦334332 I heard¦334332 rumbling¦334335 like a large¦334336 earthquake behind¦334333 me. (May Yahweh's¦334340 \add ≈honour\add* in his place¦334341 be blessed¦334337.)
\v 13 It was the sound of the living¦334346 creatures¦334346' wings¦334345 as they touched¦334347 one another, and the sound of the wheels¦334353 that were with them, and the sound of a large¦334357 earthquake.
\v 14 Then¦334359 the spirit lifted¦334360 me up and took¦334361 me away, and I¦334362 went¦334362 with¦334364 bitterness¦334363 and rage in¦334364 my spirit¦334359, because Yahweh's¦334368 hand¦334366 was pressing down firmly on¦334364 me.
\v 15 Then¦334372 I went¦334372 to the captives at¦334394 Tel¦334376-Abib who lived¦334378 along the Kebar¦334383 Canal, and¦334372 I stayed among¦334394 them there for seven¦334391 days¦334392, overwhelmed in¦334394 amazement.
\rem /s1 A Watchman for Israel; The Lord Appoints Ezekiel as a Lookout; Warning to Israel
\rem /r (Ezekiel 33.1-9)
\p
\v 16 \add ≈After those seven¦334398 days¦334399 were over\add*, Yahweh¦334404 \add gave\add* me this message¦334402:\f + \fr 3:16 \ft This formula occurs around fifty times in Ezekiel's account.\f*
\v 17 “Humanity's child, I've made you¦334412 a \add ≈guard over the Israeli¦334413 people\add*, so listen¦334415 to \add ≈this message¦334417 of mine\add* and give¦334418 them my warning¦334418.
\v 18 When I tell the wicked, ‘You'll certainly die’ and you don't¦334426 warn them \add about that\add* or give them a warning about their evil actions so they might live—the wicked will die for their sin, but¦334426 I'll¦334441 \add ≈hold you responsible for their death\add*.
\v 19 \add ≈But¦334443\add* if you do warn the wicked, and¦334443 they don't¦334448 turn from their wickedness or from their wicked actions, then¦334443 they'll die¦334456 for their sin, but¦334443 you will have saved your own life¦334460.
\p
\v 20 If a godly¦334465 person turns¦334464 from their righteousness and behaves unjustly, and I put a stumbling¦334470 block¦334470 in front¦334471 of that¦334483 person, they'll die. Because you didn't¦334475 warn them, they'll die in their sin, and I won't¦334475 consider the righteous things they did, but¦334464 I'll¦334487 \add ≈hold you responsible for their death\add*.
\v 21 \add ≈But¦334489\add* if you warn the godly¦334492 person to stop sinning so that they no longer sin, \add @that person\add* will surely live, since they were warned¦334503, and¦334489 you will have saved your own life¦334507.”
\s1 Yehezkel's calling
\rem /s1 Ezekiel Will Be Unable to Talk; Ezekiel Isolated and Silenced; The coming ruin of Jerusalem
\p
\v 22 Then Yahweh's¦334516 hand¦334514 was on me there, and he told me, “\add ≈Get ready\add* \add and\add* go¦334520 out into the plain¦334523, and I'll¦334525 speak¦334525 with you there.”
\p
\v 23 I \add ≈got up\add* and went¦334529 out into the plain¦334532 where Yahweh's¦334538 glory was staying, like the glory I'd seen¦334542 beside the Kebar¦334547 Canal, so I fell¦334548 \add ≈to my knees and bowed low to the ground\add*.
\v 24 Then¦334553 the spirit¦334556 entered¦334553 me and stood me up on¦334555 my feet¦334560, and spoke¦334561 with¦334555 me, telling me: Go and shut yourself¦334566 up in¦334555 your¦334568 house¦334568.
\v 25 Humanity's¦334571 child, \add @people\add* will \add ≈tie you up with¦334582 ropes¦334577\add* so that you'll be unable to go¦334581 \add ≈outside\add*.
\v 26 Then¦334584 I'll¦334585 make¦334585 your tongue¦334584 stick¦334585 to the roof¦334588 of your mouth¦334588, so you'll become¦334592 mute, and¦334584 although they're rebellious¦334598 \add ≈people\add*, you won't¦334590 be able to \add ≈tell them off\add*.
\v 27 \add ≈But¦334601\add* when I speak¦334601 to you, I'll¦334603 open your mouth¦334606 so you'll be able to tell them, ‘This is what the master¦334611 Yahweh¦334611 says.’ The ones who will hear will hear, \add but¦334601\add* the ones who won't listen won't listen, because¦334619 they're rebellious¦334621 \add ≈people\add*.
\c 4
\ms1 Messages about Yerushalem's destruction
\mr (4:1–24:27)
\s1 Yehezkel models Yerushalem's invasion
\rem /s1 A Sign of the Coming Siege; The Siege of Jerusalem Portrayed; Ezekiel Acts Out the Siege of Jerusalem; Siege of Jerusalem Symbolized
\p
\v 1 But¦334625 you, humanity's¦334628 child, get yourself¦334631 a brick¦334632 and place it \add ≈in front¦334635 of\add* you and carve Yerushalem¦334641 City¦334626 on it.
\v 2 Then¦334643 lay siege¦334645 against it, and build¦334646 forts against it. \add ≈Build\add* an assault ramp up against it and make camps around it. Place battering¦334658 rams all around it.
\v 3 \add ≈After that,\add* get yourself an iron pan and use it as an iron wall¦334669 between yourself and \add your representation of\add* the city¦334673, and \add keep looking in¦334680 that direction¦334674\add*, because it'll be under siege and you're to put the siege against it. That will be a sign¦334683 to the \add ≈Israeli¦334685 people\add*.
\p
\v 4 Then lie on your left side¦334693 and put the sin of the \add ≈Israeli¦334701 people\add* on it. You'll carry their¦334711 sin for the number¦334703 of days¦334704 you lie down \add as a sign\add* against them.
\v 5 I myself am assigning¦334714 to you one day to represent each year of their¦334719 punishment: 390 days¦334721 \add lying on your left side\add*. In that way, you'll carry the \add ≈Israeli¦334729 people's\add* sin.
\v 6 When¦334733 \add ≈that period is over\add*, then¦334733 lie down a second¦334744 time on your right¦334741 side, because you'll carry the sin of \add ≈Yehudah's¦334751 people\add* for forty¦334752 days. I'm¦334758 assigning¦334758 one day to you for each year.
\p
\v 7 \add ≈Keep looking\add* towards Yerushalem¦334764, which is under siege¦334763, and¦334761 with your arm bared¦334768 \add like a warrior\add*, prophesy¦334769 against¦334770 it¦334770.
\v 8 \add ≈Listen,\add* I'll¦334773 \add have you\add* tied with ropes¦334775 so you won't¦334776 be able to turn¦334778 from one side to the other until¦334783 the days¦334786 \add representing the years\add* of your¦334779 siege¦334787 are over.
\p
\v 9 Take wheat¦334793, barley¦334794, beans¦334795, lentils¦334796, millet¦334797, and spelt¦334798 for yourself, \add and\add* put them into a single container, and make bread¦334806 for yourself according to the number¦334807 of days you'll lie on¦334801 your side—\add yes,\add* you'll eat it for 390 days.
\v 10 You'll measure 250g by weight¦334827 to eat each day, and¦334824 you'll eat it during the day at¦334827 set times.
\v 11 Then¦334837 you'll measure¦334838 out half a litre of water¦334837 to drink each day, and¦334837 you'll drink it at¦334838 set times.
\v 12 You'll \add cook and¦334851\add* eat¦334850 \add @that bread¦334848\add* as barley¦334849 cakes, but¦334848 \add burn sun-dried\add* human¦334854 excrement¦334853 to bake it¦334855 over \add ≈while they're watching\add*.
\p
\v 13 Yahweh¦334860 says that that means that the bread¦334868 that the Israeli¦334865 people¦334863 will eat¦334862 there¦334873 among¦334870 the \add other\add* nations¦334870 that I'll¦334872 banish¦334872 them to will be ceremonially unclean¦334869.
\v 14 \add ≈But¦334875 I protested\add*, “Oh no, master¦334877 Yahweh¦334877. I've never \add ≈broken our dietary laws\add*. \add ≈Ever since¦334888 I was young, and right up till now,\add* I've never eaten¦334887 either anything that died¦334883 or anything killed by animals¦334884, and foul meat¦334896 has never entered my¦334880 mouth¦334895.”
\p
\v 15 So \add @Yahweh\add* \add ≈answered\add* me, “Listen, I'll give¦334903 you cow manure instead of human¦334912 excrement, so you can \add ≈bake\add* your¦334916 bread¦334916 over that¦334917.”
\p
\v 16 Then he told me, “Humanity's child, listen. I'm breaking¦334926 the \add ≈cycle of food¦334929 supply\add* in¦334930 Yerushalem¦334930, and they'll eat bread while anxiously rationing it, and drink¦334939 water¦334936 while fearfully rationing it,
\v 17 \add ≈because\add* they'll lack \add both\add* food¦334943 and water¦334944, and everyone¦334946 will be appalled¦334945 by their¦334949 \add ≈neighbours' actions,\add* and they'll waste¦334948 away because they \add ≈disobeyed\add* \add God\add*.
\c 5
\s1 Yehezkel's Yerushalem model
\rem /s1 A Sword against Jerusalem; A Sign of the Coming Judgment; Ezekiel Cuts His Hair
\p
\v 1 Then¦334953 you, humanity's¦334955 child, take a sharp¦334961 sword¦334960 as a barber's¦334963 razor¦334962 for yourself¦334965, and \add ≈use it to shave¦334966\add* your head¦334969 and beard¦334972, then get \add some\add* scales \add ≈so you can\add* weigh¦334976 your hair and divide¦334977 \add *it\add* \add equally into three piles\add*.
\v 2 Burn a third of it in¦334980 the middle¦334982 of the city when the days \add representing\add* the siege¦334986 have finished¦334984, and take \add ≈the second pile\add* of hair and hit it with¦334980 the sword all around¦334993 the city. Then scatter \add the final\add* third to the wind, and I'll¦334998 draw out a sword to chase after¦334999 the people.
\v 3 \add ≈But¦335001\add* take¦335001 a few hairs from them and¦335005 tie them into the folds of your¦335007 robe¦335007.
\v 4 Then¦335009 take \add a bit\add* more of the hair and¦335009 throw¦335012 it into the middle¦335016 of the fire \add ≈to be burnt up\add*—from there a fire will spread out to all the \add ≈Israeli¦335030 people\add*.”
\p
\v 5 My master¦335035 Yahweh¦335035 says¦335034, “That \add brick model\add* is Yerushalem¦335038 where I've placed her in the middle¦335039 of the nations¦335040, and¦335042 where I've surrounded her with other \add ≈countries¦335040\add*.
\v 6 \add ≈But¦335045 due to her wickedness¦335049,\add* she's rejected my decrees more than \add other\add* nations¦335052 have, and \add ≡avoided\add* my regulations more than the countries¦335058 that¦335059 surround her. Her¦335060 people have rejected my judgements and haven't \add ≈followed\add* my regulations.”
\v 7 Therefore my master¦335076 Yahweh¦335076 says this, “Because you're more troublesome than the nations that¦335083 surround you, and haven't \add ≈followed\add* my statutes or obeyed my regulations¦335085, or even acted according¦335093 to the surrounding nations' regulations,”
\v 8 therefore my master¦335104 Yahweh¦335104 says¦335103 this, “Listen, I myself will work against¦335107 you. I'll¦335111 execute¦335111 judgements¦335113 among you for the \add other\add* nations¦335115 to see¦335106.
\v 9 Because of your¦335135 detestable actions, I'll do things to you¦335118 that¦335120 I've¦335123 never done before, and¦335124 which I'll never do again¦335131:
