\v 10 \add ≈So¦336154\add* I went through and looked¦336155, and oh dear, there were shapes of every¦336157 creeping¦336160 thing and detestable¦336162 creature. \add Pictures of\add* all the \add ≈Israeli¦336166 people's\add* idols¦336165 were carved¦336168 into the wall all around.
\v 11 Seventy elders¦336178 from the \add ≈Israeli¦336179 people\add* were there, and Shafan's¦336185 son Yaazanyah¦336182 was standing in the middle of them. They were standing in front¦336189 of the images, and each man¦336177 \add ≈was holding\add* his incense burner so that the smell of the cloud¦336194 of incense went up.
\v 12 Then¦336199 he \add ≈asked\add* me, “Humanity's child, do you see what the \add ≈Israeli¦336207\add* elders¦336206 are doing¦336210 in the dark? Each one does this in his idol's¦336214 hidden room¦336213, because¦336215 they say, ‘Yahweh doesn't \add even\add* \add ≈notice\add* us. Yahweh's¦336218 \add ≈abandoned¦336221 this country\add*.’ ”
\p
\v 13 Then¦336227 he told me, “Turn again¦336229 and¦336227 see¦336231 the other \add ≈terribly disgusting things\add* that¦336234 they're doing¦336237,”
\v 14 and he took me to the gate¦336244 at the northern¦336251 entrance¦336243 of Yahweh's¦336247 temple, and oh dear—there were some women¦336255 sitting¦336256 there mourning for the \add Babylonian¦336252\add* Tammuz¦336260 \add deity\add*.
