\p
\v 16 Then¦336276 he took me into the inner¦336284 courtyard¦336280 of Yahweh's house¦336281, and oh no—at the entrance¦336287 of Yahweh's temple between the porch¦336291 and the altar¦336293, there were about¦336294 twenty-five men with their backs¦336297 toward the temple and their faces¦336302 toward the east \add ≈where\add* they were worshipping the sun¦336307.
\p
\v 17 He \add ≈asked\add* me, “Humanity's child, do you see¦336335 that? Is it insignificant that Yehudah's¦336317 \add ≈people\add* do those \add ≈disgusting things\add* that they're doing¦336318 here? They've filled¦336328 the land with violence¦336332 and keep provoking¦336334 me to anger¦336334 and \add ?≈mocking me\add*.
