\v 6 Slaughter all the old men, young¦336475 adults, little¦336477 children¦336477, and women¦336478, \add ≈but¦336476\add* don't¦336490 approach anyone who has the mark on¦336496 their head. Begin at¦336496 my \add ≈sacred place\add*.” So they began¦336495 with¦336496 the elders¦336497 who were in¦336496 front¦336499 of the \add ≈temple\add*.
\p
\v 7 \add @Yahweh\add* told them, “Defile the \add ≈temple\add*, and fill¦336508 its courtyards¦336511 with¦336516 the corpses. \add ≈Now go¦336513\add*.” So¦336502 they went¦336514 out and \add started\add* attacking the city¦336516.
\p
\v 8 As they were attacking it, I found myself alone, and I fell¦336522 \add ≈to my knees with¦336538 my head bowed down to the ground\add*, and cried¦336526 out, and said¦336527, “Ah, master¦336529 Yahweh¦336529, will you destroy¦336531 the entire¦336534 remnant¦336536 of Yisrael¦336537 \add ≈by pouring out\add* your rage¦336541 on¦336538 Yerushalem¦336544?”
\p
\v 9 “The disobedience of the \add ≈people\add* of Yisrael¦336551 and Yehudah has been \add ≈extremely bad\add*,” he answered. “The land is full of blood¦336558, and the city¦336559 full of perversions¦336561, since they say, ‘Yahweh has forgotten \add ≈this country\add*,’ and ‘Yahweh won't¦336569 \add ≈take any notice\add*.’
\v 10 So¦336573 then¦336573, \add ≈I won't show¦336581\add* compassion¦336578, and¦336573 I won't spare them, rather I'll¦336581 bring it¦336578 all on¦336583 their heads¦336583.”
\p
\v 11 Then¦336586 wow, the man¦336587 dressed in¦336593 linen¦336590 who had the writing¦336592 equipment by his side came back to report, saying, “I've¦336597 done¦336597 everything you¦336601 commanded¦336601.”
