\v 5 The sound¦336688 of the creatures' wings¦336689 could be heard¦336691 as far as the outer¦336695 courtyard¦336694, like the voice¦336696 of the powerful God¦336697 when he speaks¦336700.
\p
\v 6 When¦336702 \add @Yahweh\add* had commanded¦336703 the man dressed in linen¦336709, “Take fire¦336712 from between the wheels that are between the winged creatures,” the man went in and¦336702 stood¦336718 beside¦336719 a wheel.
\v 7 A winged creature reached out his hand¦336726 between¦336733 the winged creatures to the fire¦336731 that¦336732 was among¦336727 \add *them\add*, and lifted¦336735 it up and placed it into the hands¦336739 of the one dressed in linen¦336741. The man¦336740 took¦336742 it and went¦336743 back out.
\p
\v 8 I \add ≈noticed\add* that the winged creatures had something like a human¦336750 hand¦336748 under¦336751 their¦336752 wings¦336752,
\v 9 then¦336754 I looked¦336754, and wow, four¦336756 wheels were beside the winged creatures—one wheel beside each \add *one\add*—and the wheels seemed like shining chrysolite¦336774.\x + \xo 10:9-13: \xt Eze 1:15-21.\x*
\v 10 \add *They\add* all appeared¦336776 to be the same, like having a wheel within a wheel.
\v 11 When they moved, they went in any of their¦336790 four¦336789 directions, without turning as they went, because¦336795 whatever direction the head¦336800 faced, they went in that¦336797 direction without turning as they went.
\v 12 Their¦336817 whole body¦336809 (including¦336810 their backs¦336810, their hands¦336811, and their wings¦336812) was covered with eyes, and there were eyes all around¦336816 the four wheels, covering them as well.\x + \xo 10:12: \xt Rev 4:8.\x*
\v 13 I heard \add someone\add* call them ‘the whirling wheels¦336820’.
\p
\v 14 Each one had four faces¦336827: the first face was a winged creature's face, the second¦336834 was a human¦336836 face, the third¦336837 was a lion's face, and¦336826 the fourth¦336840 was an eagle's¦336843 face.\x + \xo 10:14: \xt Eze 1:10; Rev 4:7.\x*
\v 15 Then¦336845 the living¦336848 creatures (they¦336845 were the same ones I'd¦336850 seen¦336850 by the Kebar¦336853 Canal) rose up \add in¦336851 the air\add*.
\v 16 Whenever the winged creatures moved, the wheels would go beside them, and¦336855 whenever the winged creatures lifted¦336860 up their¦336864 wings¦336864 to take off from the earth¦336867, the wheels didn't¦336868 turn—they still stayed beside them.
\v 17 When the winged creatures stood still, the wheels stood still, and when they went up, the wheels went up with¦336879 them, because¦336882 the spirit¦336883 of the living¦336884 creature was in¦336879 the wheels.
\p
\v 18 Then¦336887 Yahweh's¦336889 \add ≈brilliant light\add* moved¦336887 out over the \add ≈temple\add* threshold¦336891 and¦336893 stayed over the winged creatures.
\v 19 The winged creatures lifted¦336898 up their¦336902 wings¦336902 and rose from the ground in¦336908 my sight when they¦336908 travelled¦336908, and the wheels¦336909 did the same beside them. They stood¦336911 at¦336908 the eastern¦336917 entrance¦336912 to Yahweh's¦336916 residence, and the \add ≈brilliant light\add* of Yisrael's god¦336919 came onto them from above¦336923.
\v 20 Those were the living¦336926 creatures that I'd seen¦336928 below Yisrael's god¦336930 by the Kebar¦336935 Canal, so I knew¦336936 that they¦336939 were winged creatures.
\p
\v 21 They each had four faces¦336943 and four wings, and had something like human¦336950 hands¦336949 under¦336951 their¦336952 wings,
\v 22 and their faces \add ≈resembled\add* the faces that¦336958 I'd seen in the vision at the Kebar¦336964 Canal, and each of them went straight ahead.
\c 11
\s1 Yahweh's punishment for Yerushalem
\rem /s1 Judgment on Wicked Counsellors; Judgment on Israel's Leaders; Jerusalem Is Condemned
\p
\v 1 Then¦336974 the spirit¦336976 lifted¦336974 me up and brought¦336977 me to the eastern¦336985 gate of Yahweh's¦336984 \add ≈temple\add*, facing east, and wow, in¦336989 the doorway of the gate there were twenty-five men. Among them I saw¦336994 Azzur's¦337001 son Yaazanyah¦336998 and Benayah's¦337007 son Felatyah, \add who were\add* leaders¦337008 of the people¦337009.
\p
\v 2 \add @Yahweh\add* told me, “Humanity's¦337014 child, these¦337017 are the men¦337018 who \add ≈plan to do evil¦337024 things\add* and who make wicked¦337020 plans in¦337025 this city¦337025.
\v 3 They're saying, ‘\add ≈This isn't¦337029 yet\add* the time to build¦337031 houses¦337032. This city is \add like a cooking\add* pot, and¦337035 we're the meat.’
\v 4 So¦337042, prophesy against¦337040 them, humanity's¦337044 child, \add start\add* prophesying.”
\p
\v 5 Then¦337046 Yahweh's¦337049 spirit¦337048 came on me and¦337046 told me to say¦337052: This is what Yahweh says¦337055, “That's what you Israeli¦337060 \add ≈people\add* are saying, because I know¦337064 what goes through your¦337062 mind.
\v 6 You've killed \add ≈many people\add* in¦337068 this city¦337068, and¦337070 filled¦337070 its¦337071 streets¦337071 with¦337068 them.
\p
\v 7 Therefore the master¦337079 Yahweh¦337079 says¦337078: The people you've killed, whose bodies you've laid in¦337084 the middle of Yerushalem, are the meat, and this city is the pot. But¦337087 you \add people\add* are going to be brought out from the centre of this city.
\v 8 You've feared¦337094 the sword, so I'm bringing¦337096 the sword against¦337097 you. That's my master¦337099 Yahweh's¦337100 declaration.
\v 9 I'll bring you out from the city, and¦337102 put you into the hands¦337107 of foreigners, because I'll bring judgement¦337112 against you \add people\add*.
\v 10 You'll \add ≈be killed\add* by the sword¦337114. I'll¦337120 judge¦337120 you within Yisrael's borders so that you \add people\add* will know¦337122 that I am Yahweh¦337126.
\v 11 This city won't¦337129 be your cooking pot, nor will you be the meat inside it. I'll¦337142 judge¦337142 you \add people\add* within Yisrael's borders¦337140.
\v 12 Then¦337145 you'll know¦337145 that I am Yahweh¦337149, the one whose instructions¦337151 you haven't \add ≈obeyed\add* and¦337145 whose regulations¦337151 you haven't \add ≈followed\add*. Instead, you people have \add imitated\add* the \add wicked\add* \add ≈customs\add* of the nations¦337158 that surround you.”
\p
\v 13 Then¦337163 as I was prophesying¦337164, Benayah's¦337168 son Felatyah died¦337169. \add ≈So¦337163\add* I fell¦337170 \add ≈to my knees with my face¦337173 bowed low to the ground\add* and¦337163 cried¦337174 out with a loud voice¦337175, “Oh no, my master¦337180 Yahweh¦337180, will you¦337183 completely¦337182 \add ≈eliminate the Israeli¦337186 people\add*?”
\s1 Yahweh's promise to the exiles
\rem /s1 Hope for Exiled Israel; God's Promise to the Exiles; God Will Restore Israel
\p
\v 14 Then Yahweh¦337193 \add ≈gave me this\add* message¦337191:
\v 15 “Your brothers, humanity's¦337199 child, your brothers and all the \add ≈Israeli¦337206 people¦337202 who were exiled¦337203\add*—the ones living in Yerushalem¦337213 say about them all, ‘They're far away from Yahweh¦337216. \em This land\em* was given¦337219 to us as \add ≈ours to own¦337221\add*.’
\rem /s1 Promised Return of Israel
\p
\v 16 So tell \add them\add*, ‘My master¦337229 Yahweh¦337229 says¦337228 this: ‘Although I've removed¦337232 them far away \add ≈to other\add* nations¦337233, and though I've scattered¦337235 them among \add &those\add* lands, I myself have been a \add ≈place of security\add* for them for a little¦337240 while in¦337233 the lands where¦337242 they¦337244 \add ≈were taken\add*.’
\p
\v 17 So \add explain\add* \add to them\add*, ‘My master¦337253 Yahweh¦337253 says¦337252 this: ‘I'll gather¦337255 you from the people¦337259 groups, and assemble¦337260 you from the lands¦337264 where you were scattered¦337266, and I'll give¦337268 you \add back\add* the \add ≈country¦337264\add* of Yisrael¦337273.’
\v 18 Then¦337275 they'll go there and remove¦337278 every detestable¦337283 and disgusting thing¦337283 from there,
\v 19 and I'll give them one heart, and I'll put a new spirit¦337295 in¦337298 them. I'll take the \add ≈rock-hard¦337301\add* heart out of \add ≈them\add* and give them \add ≈a tender heart\add*,\x + \xo 11:19-20: \xt Eze 36:26-28.\x*
\v 20 so that they'll \add ≈follow my instructions¦337309 and obey my regulations¦337309\add*. Then¦337321 they'll be my people¦337320, and I'll¦337322 be their god¦337324.
\v 21 \add ≈But¦337326\add* to those who \add ≈would rather happily choose\add* their detestable¦337329 and¦337326 disgusting ways, I'll¦337335 \add ≈make their actions bounce back\add* onto their own heads¦337334. That's the master¦337337 Yahweh's¦337338 declaration.”
\s1 God's glory leaves Yerushalem
\rem /s1 The Lord's Glory Leaves Jerusalem; God's Glory Leaves Jerusalem
\p
\v 22 Then¦337340 the winged creatures lifted¦337340 up their¦337344 wings¦337344 and the wheels¦337345 that were beside¦337346 them, and the \add ≈brilliant light\add* of Yisrael's¦337350 god¦337348 was up high over them.\x + \xo 11:22-23: \xt Eze 43:2-5.\x*
\v 23 Then¦337356 \add *it\add* went up from the centre of the city and¦337354 \add ≈sat above\add* the mountain¦337363 to the east of the city.
\v 24 The spirit lifted¦337369 me up and brought¦337370 me into Chaldea¦337371 \add (Babylonia)\add* to the exiles¦337374, in¦337375 the vision from God's spirit, and the vision that¦337381 I'd been seeing left me,
\v 25 and¦337384 I told the exiles¦337387 everything Yahweh¦337392 had shown¦337394 me.
\c 12
\s1 Portraying the future exile
\rem /s1 The Exile Symbolized; The Prophet as a Refugee; Judah's Captivity Portrayed; The false prophets; Signs of the Coming Exile
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦337400 \add ≈gave me this\add* message¦337398:
\v 2 “Humanity's child, you live among a rebellious \add ≈people group\add* who have eyes¦337414 to see, yet they don't see, and who have ears¦337419 to hear, but¦337417 don't listen¦337421, because¦337424 they're a rebellious \add ≈people group\add*.\x + \xo 12:2: \xt Isa 6:9-10; Jer 5:21; Mrk 8:18.\x*
\p
\v 3 “Therefore, humanity's¦337432 child, \add ≈pack up your stuff ready to go into\add* exile, and¦337429 \add ≈each day¦337438 while they're watching\add*, start going out \add somewhere\add*, because¦337449 \add ≈while they're watching\add*, I'll exile you from your place to another¦337445 place. Perhaps they'll begin to see, even though they're \add such\add* rebellious¦337451 \add ≈people\add*.
\v 4 \add ≈Each day¦337458 while they're watching,\add* bring¦337454 out your¦337455 things for an exile, \add then¦337454\add* as they watch in the evening¦337462, go¦337461 out in the way that \add ≈people do\add* when going¦337464 into exile.
\v 5 Dig a hole through the \add city\add* wall¦337471 \add ≈where they'll see you do it\add*, and¦337472 go out through it.
\v 6 \add ≈While they're watching\add*, lift your things up onto your shoulder¦337478, and bring¦337481 them out in¦337480 the darkness¦337480. Cover your face¦337482, because¦337489 you mustn't see¦337485 \add &this\add* land, since I've¦337492 \add ≈made¦337492 you into\add* a sign¦337491 for the \add ≈Israeli¦337493 people\add*.”
\p
\v 7 So¦337496 I did just as I was instructed¦337499: I brought my things for an exile¦337503 out in the daytime, and in the evening¦337505 I dug a hole through the wall¦337509 by hand¦337510. I brought my things out in the dark, and lifted¦337516 them up onto my shoulder¦337515 \add ≈as they watched\add*.
\rem Need to make next verse style consistent throughout the document: Yahweh GAVE ME a message, vs Yahweh's message CAME TO ME.
\p
\v 8 The \add next\add* morning¦337525, Yahweh¦337523 \add ≈gave me this\add* message¦337521:
\v 9 “Humanity's¦337535 child, haven't those rebellious¦337537 \add ≈Israeli¦337534 people\add* asked you what you're doing¦337540?
\v 10 Tell them that the master¦337546 Yahweh¦337546 says¦337545 this: ‘this prophetic action concerns the ruler in¦337551 Yerushalem¦337551 and¦337553 all the \add other\add* \add ≈Israeli¦337555 people\add* who are there.’
\v 11 Tell them that you're a sign¦337564 to them, and that everything you've done will happen to them—they'll be \add ≈captured and taken into exile¦337570\add* \add in¦337570 another country\add*.
\v 12 \add ≈Their¦337577 leader\add* will lift his things up onto his shoulder¦337580 in¦337577 the dark, and will go¦337583 out through the wall. They'll dig through the wall and take their¦337577 things out. He'll cover¦337589 his face, so he won't¦337592 see¦337594 the \add ≈place\add* \add he's leaving\add*.
\v 13 I'll spread¦337602 my net¦337605 out over him and he'll be caught¦337607 in¦337608 my trap, then¦337602 I'll take him \add away\add* to Babylon¦337611 (the land¦337612 of the Chaldeans), but¦337602 he won't¦337615 see¦337617 it, and he'll die¦337619 there¦337618.\x + \xo 12:13: \xt 2Ki 25:7; Jer 52:11.\x*
\v 14 I'll also scatter all of his assistants in every direction, and¦337621 I'll send out a sword¦337633 after¦337635 his entire¦337626 army.
\v 15 When¦337637 I scatter¦337645 them among the nations¦337644 and¦337645 disperse¦337642 them throughout the lands¦337647, then¦337637 they'll know¦337637 that I am Yahweh¦337641.
\v 16 \add ≈But¦337649\add* I'll¦337649 spare¦337649 a few of them from the sword¦337653, famine¦337654, and plague¦337655, so they'll be able to record all their¦337662 \add ≈hardships and ungodly practices\add* in¦337663 the \add ≈countries¦337663\add* that I take them to, so they'll know¦337668 that I am Yahweh¦337672.”
\s1 Portraying the peoples' trembling
\rem /s1 The Sign of the Trembling Prophet; Judgment Not Postponed
\p
\v 17 Then Yahweh¦337678 \add ≈gave me\add* \add another\add* message¦337676:
\v 18 “Humanity's child, eat¦337687 your food \add ≈while trembling¦337689 with¦337686 fear\add*, and drink¦337691 your water¦337688 \add ≈while shaking anxiously\add*,
\v 19 and tell the people¦337696 in¦337710 \add ≈this country\add*, ‘My master¦337701 Yahweh¦337701 says¦337700 this about the inhabitants¦337703 of Yerushalem¦337704, and the \add ≈country\add* of Yisrael¦337708, “They'll anxiously eat¦337711 their food and fearfully drink¦337714 their water¦337712, since \add ≈all the abundance from the land will be devastated\add* because¦337719 of the violence¦337719 of all \add the people\add* who live¦337722 there.
\v 20 The inhabited¦337726 cities¦337725 will become desolate¦337729, and¦337725 the land \add itself\add* will become a wasteland¦337727. Then¦337725 you'll know that I am Yahweh¦337735.” ’ ”
\s1 Just because it never came true before…
\rem /s1 A Popular Proverb and an Unpopular Message; A New Proverb for Israel
\p
\v 21 Then Yahweh¦337741 \add ≈gave me\add* \add another\add* message¦337739:
\v 22 “Humanity's child, what's that saying that you¦337752 have in Yisrael¦337756? It goes, ‘The days¦337759 \add ≈seem to go on and on, yet no prophecy ever comes¦337760 true.\add*’
\v 23 So tell them, ‘This is what the master¦337771 Yahweh¦337771 says¦337770: I'm going to prove that what they say isn't¦337778 correct, then they'll never say it again¦337782 in¦337783 Yisrael¦337783.’ Tell them, ‘It'll soon be the time¦337790 when everything¦337792 that the prophets have predicted will happen,
\v 24 because there'll no longer be any false visions¦337802 or \add ≈people-pleasing prophecies\add* within Yisrael¦337808.
\v 25 I speak, and I \add ≈put the words that¦337816 I speak into action\add*, because I am Yahweh. The matter will no longer be delayed, because I'll speak this message¦337818 in¦337824 your \add ≈lifetimes\add*, \add you\add* rebellious¦337826 \add ≈people\add*, and then I'll carry it out!’ That's the master¦337831 Yahweh's¦337813 declaration.”
\p
\v 26 Then Yahweh¦337838 \add ≈gave me\add* \add another\add* message¦337836:
\v 27 “Listen, humanity's¦337844 child, the \add ≈Israeli¦337846 people\add* have said¦337849, ‘The vision¦337850 that¦337851 \add @the prophet\add* sees is for many years¦337855 from now, and he prophesies about far-off times¦337857,’
\v 28 so tell them, ‘The master Yahweh¦337867 says this: ‘My words¦337875 won't¦337869 be delayed any longer, but¦337879 the message¦337878 that¦337876 I've given will be \add ≈put into effect\add*. That's the master Yahweh's¦337868 declaration.’ ”
\c 13
\s1 Condemning the false prophets
\rem /s1 Prophecy against False Male Prophets; False Prophets Condemned; Judgment against False Prophets
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦337888 \add ≈gave me\add* \add another\add* message¦337886:
\v 2 “Humanity's child, prophesy against¦337896 the prophets who are prophesying in Yisrael¦337899, and¦337901 tell those who are prophesying out of their¦337903 own imaginations¦337903, ‘Listen to Yahweh's¦337907 message¦337905.
\v 3 My master¦337911 Yahweh¦337911 says¦337910 this: ‘Foolish prophets¦337916 who follow their¦337921 own spirit¦337921 and¦337922 haven't \add actually\add* seen¦337923 any \add vision\add* \add ≈won't¦337922 end well\add*.
\v 4 Yisrael¦337928, your¦337927 prophets¦337927 have been like jackals¦337925 in¦337926 the wastelands.
\v 5 You¦337939 haven't gone to the breaks in the \add #walls\add* around the Israeli¦337938 \add cities\add* and repaired¦337934 them, in order to \add ≈be able to defend yourselves well during\add* the battle¦337941 on¦337933 Yahweh's¦337943 \add chosen\add* day¦337942.
\v 6 The people have false visions and make false predictions. Yahweh hasn't sent¦337955 those¦337949 who say¦337949 that they're bringing Yahweh's¦337952 declaration, \add ≈but¦337947 nevertheless they've made people hope that their messages¦337958 would come true\add*.
\v 7 Haven't you had false visions¦337961 and made false predictions—all of you who say that you're bringing Yahweh's¦337971 declaration when I myself haven't spoken¦337974?’
\p
\v 8 Therefore the master Yahweh says this, ‘Because you \add people\add* have \add ≈presented\add* false¦337986 visions and have told lies, this is the master Yahweh's¦337981 declaration against¦337989 you:
\v 9 \add ≈I'll punish\add* the prophets¦337998 who have lying visions¦337999 and¦337994 who make false¦338002 predictions. They won't¦338005 be \add allowed\add* in the assembly of my people¦338004, or enrolled in the record of Yisrael's \add ≈descendants\add*. They mustn't go¦338019 to the land¦338016 of Yisrael¦338011—\add ≈that's how\add* you \add people\add* will know¦338020 that I am the master¦338023 Yahweh¦338023.
\p
\v 10 Also because¦338027 they led my people¦338031 astray¦338028 and said, “Peace,” when there's¦338034 no peace, \add it's as if\add* they're building¦338037 a wall and then whitewashing¦338042 it.’\x + \xo 13:10: \xt Jer 6:14; 8:11.\x*
\v 11 Tell the ones who are whitewashing¦338048 the wall¦338060 that it'll fall down. There'll be a downpour, then I'll send hailstones to make it fall down, and a strong wind to break¦338060 it down.
\v 12 See, the wall¦338064 will fall down. Haven't others \add ≈asked\add* you where¦338068 the white¦338069 coating \add went\add* that¦338070 you put on it?
\p
\v 13 Therefore my master¦338077 Yahweh¦338077 says this: ‘In my rage, I'll¦338079 bring a storm, and in¦338083 my anger¦338086, there'll be \add ≈heavy rain causing floods\add*. In my rage, hailstones will completely¦338091 destroy¦338091 \add @Yerushalem\add*.
\v 14 I'll tear down the wall¦338096 that you covered with¦338109 whitewash¦338100, and I'll demolish it to ground level and expose its¦338109 foundations¦338106. So¦338093 it'll fall¦338107, and you'll be annihilated in¦338109 the middle of it all. Then¦338093 you \add people\add* will know¦338110 that I am Yahweh¦338114.
\p
\v 15 In my rage¦338119 I'll annihilate the wall and¦338116 those¦338129 who whitewashed it. I'll tell you, “The wall doesn't exist anymore, nor do the people who whitewashed it—
\v 16 those Israeli¦338132 prophets who prophesied about Yerushalem¦338138 and had visions¦338141 of peace for it. But¦338139 there¦338143 isn't¦338143 any peace! That's¦338133 the master¦338146 Yahweh's¦338147 declaration.” ’
\rem /s1 Prophecy against False Female Prophets; Judgment against False Women Prophets
\p
\v 17 \add ≈So¦338151\add*, humanity's¦338153 child, \add ≈turn your attention to\add* your people's¦338159 daughters¦338158 and prophesy against¦338156 them \add ≈because they invented prophecies in their¦338161 own imaginations¦338161\add*.
\v 18 Tell \add >them\add* that the master¦338170 Yahweh¦338170 says this: ‘The women \add ≈won't end well\add* who sew magic charms onto every part of their hands¦338180, and make headbands for people of \add ≈every walk of life\add* \add that are used to deceive people and\add* hunt them down. \add Do you people really think you can get away with\add* hunting down my people, but¦338165 then¦338165 save your own lives?
\v 19 You've profaned¦338198 me among my people for handfuls¦338204 of barley¦338205 and crumbs of bread¦338207. \add ≡You people have\add* killed people who shouldn't have died, and saved the lives of those who shouldn't have continued to live, because of your lies to my people who heard you.
\p
\v 20 Therefore my master¦338231 Yahweh¦338231 says¦338229 this: ‘I'm against¦338234 the magic¦338236 charms that¦338237 you've used to \add ≈lure\add* the people in as if they were birds. Indeed, I'll tear them from your arms, and I'll let the people you've trapped like birds go free.
\v 21 I'll¦338261 tear away your headbands and¦338261 rescue¦338265 my people¦338268 from your \add ≈control\add* so they'll no longer be trapped in¦338274 your \add ≈system\add*. Then¦338261 you \add people\add* will know¦338276 that I am Yahweh¦338280.
\p
\v 22 Because¦338282 you've discouraged the righteous¦338286 people with lies (even though I¦338288 didn't¦338289 desire their discouragement), and because you \add people\add* \add ≈encouraged the actions\add* of the wicked¦338293 people instead so they won't¦338289 change¦338296 their ways¦338297 to save¦338299 their lives¦338299,
\v 23 \add ≈because of that\add*, you'll no longer have false visions¦338305 or continue to make predictions, because I'll¦338310 rescue¦338310 my people¦338313 out of your¦338314 \add ≈control\add*. Then you'll know¦338315 that I am Yahweh¦338319.’ ”
\c 14
\s1 Yahweh's hate for idols
\rem /s1 Idolaters Condemned; God's Judgments Justified; God Condemns Idolatry; The Idolatry of Israel's Leaders
\p
\v 1 \add ≈One day\add* \add some\add* of the Israeli¦338325 elders¦338324 came¦338321 and¦338326 sat down \add to talk\add*,
\v 2 and¦338330 Yahweh¦338333 \add ≈gave\add* me this message¦338331:
\v 3 “Humanity's child, these¦338341 men¦338340 have taken their idols¦338343 \add ≈to be their gods\add*, and \add ≈their choice to disobey makes it very difficult for them to relate to me\add*. Should I \add ≈even let them ask me anything\add*?
\p
\v 4 Therefore tell them that the master¦338367 Yahweh says this: ‘Every Israeli¦338372 person who \add ≈makes their idols their priority\add*, or who \add ≈allows their disobedience to separate them from me\add*, and who then comes¦338386 to a prophet¦338389, I, Yahweh, will answer¦338392 them according to \add ≈how many idols they have\add*.
\v 5 I'll do that so that I can \add ≈reclaim the Israeli¦338403 people whose values are now far from mine due to\add* their¦338411 idols¦338410.
\p
\v 6 Therefore tell the Israeli¦338420 people that the master¦338423 Yahweh¦338423 says¦338422 this: ‘\add ≈Change your behaviour\add* and turn away from your idols¦338428. \add ≈Make a decision to stop disobeying me by doing those evil things\add*.
\p
\v 7 Any \add ≈Israeli¦338440 person\add* or any foreigner residing in¦338445 Yisrael¦338440 who deserts me, who takes idols¦338449 \add ≈to be their gods\add* and \add ≈allows their disobedience to separate¦338446 them from me\add*, and who then comes¦338458 to a prophet¦338461 to \add ≈request my guidance\add*, I, Yahweh¦338467, will answer¦338468 that person myself¦338468.
\v 8 I'll¦338473 \add ≈clearly show my disapproval\add* and make¦338477 that person¦338475 into a sign¦338478 \add for others\add* and into a \add ≈talking point\add*, and they'll be \add ≈isolated from the rest of\add* my people¦338482, and you \add people\add* will know¦338483 that I am Yahweh¦338487.
\p
\v 9 If a prophet is deceived and speaks¦338494 a message¦338495, then I, Yahweh¦338497, will deceive that prophet. I'll¦338502 \add ≈take action\add* against him and destroy¦338507 him \add to remove him\add* from among¦338508 the Israeli people¦338509.
\v 10 \add ≈Both the prophet¦338517 and the one who asks him for advice will be guilty, and I'll punish both of them for their¦338513 disobedience.\add*
\v 11 Because of that, the Israeli¦338525 people will no longer wander¦338523 away from following¦338528 me, nor defile themselves¦338531 any longer through all their \add ≈disobedience\add*. They'll be my people, and I'll¦338540 be their god¦338542. That's the master¦338544 Yahweh's¦338545 declaration.’ ”
\s1 Turning the country into wasteland
\rem /s1 Judgment Inescapable; Noah, Daniel, and Job; The Certainty of the Lord's Judgment
\p
\v 12 Then Yahweh¦338551 \add ≈gave\add* me \add another\add* message¦338549:
\v 13 “Humanity's child, when a \add ≈country\add* sins against me by \add ≈choosing to worship other gods\add*, so that I \add ≈decide to take action\add* against it, \add ≈then\add* I'll break¦338569 the \add ≈cycle of food¦338573 production\add* and send¦338574 a famine¦338577 out over it. I'll \add ≈punish\add* both people and animals¦338581 from that land¦338558
\v 14 \add in such a way that\add* even if Noah¦338588, Daniel, and¦338583 Yob¦338592 \add (Job)\add* \add ≈lived in that place\add*, they could only rescue¦338595 their own lives¦338596 by being \add ≈blameless in my sight\add*. That's the master¦338598 Yahweh's¦338599 declaration.
\p
\v 15 If I send \add ≈vicious wild¦338604 animals\add* through the \add ≈country\add* and make¦338607 it barren so that it becomes¦338608 a wasteland where no one can pass¦338605 through because of those animals,
\v 16 then even if those same three¦338615 men¦338616 were in¦338618 it, as I¦338624 live, declares the master¦338623 Yahweh¦338623, they wouldn't be able to rescue¦338631 even their own \add ≈children\add*—only their own lives would be saved, but¦338628 the land \add itself\add* would become a wasteland.
\p
\v 17 Or if I bring¦338641 a sword against that \add ≈country\add* and say, ‘Sword, go through the land and \add ≈eliminate both the\add* people and \add domestic\add* animals¦338653 from it’,
\v 18 then¦338655 even if those three¦338655 men¦338656 were in¦338658 it¦338658, as I¦338664 live, declares the master¦338663 Yahweh¦338663, they wouldn't be able to rescue¦338666 even their own sons¦338667 or daughters¦338668—only their own lives would be saved.
\p
\v 19 Or if I send¦338676 a plague against that \add ≈country\add* and pour¦338681 out my rage¦338682 against it through bloodshed¦338684, in¦338684 order to \add ≈eliminate both the\add* people and the \add domestic\add* animals¦338688,
\v 20 as surely as I live, even if Noah, Daniel, and Yob¦338694 were in that country, they wouldn't be able to rescue¦338708 even their sons and daughters¦338707. They'd save only themselves by being \add ≈blameless in my¦338698 sight\add*. That's the master¦338700 Yahweh's¦338701 declaration.
\p
\v 21 The¦338719 master¦338718 Yahweh¦338718 says¦338717 this: ‘I'll¦338732 certainly make things worse by sending my four¦338723 punishments against¦338733 Yerushalem¦338735 to \add ≈eliminate both the\add* people and the \add domestic\add* animals from it: famine¦338728, sword¦338727, wild¦338730 animals, and plague¦338731.\x + \xo 14:21: \xt Rev 6:8.\x*
\v 22 \add ≈But¦338741 listen!\add* \add Despite that,\add* a remnant¦338745 will be left in¦338744 \add @the city\add*—survivors who'll go out with¦338744 sons¦338747 and daughters¦338748. \add ≈Yes,\add* they'll go out to you, and you'll see¦338752 their behaviour and actions¦338758 and \add ≈understand why they deserved\add* the punishment that I sent to Yerushalem¦338767, and about¦338750 everything else that I've¦338764 sent against the \add ≈country\add*.
\v 23 The survivors will relieve you \add people\add* when you see¦338779 their behaviour and¦338775 their actions¦338785, because¦338777 you'll know¦338786 that all those things that I've¦338790 done against \add @Yerushalem\add*, I \add ≈didn't¦338788 do them without¦338789 good reason\add*. That's the master¦338799 Yahweh's¦338800 declaration.”
\c 15
\s1 The vine stem is useless as wood
\rem /s1 A Parable about a Vine; The people and their leaders condemned; Jerusalem—a Useless Vine; The Useless Vine; Jerusalem, A Useless Vine
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦338806 \add ≈gave\add* me \add another\add* message¦338804:
\v 2 “Humanity's child, how is a vine¦338818 better than any tree¦338821 with¦338825 branches¦338822 in¦338825 a forest¦338826?
\v 3 Do people¦338835 take¦338835 wood from \add @a vine\add* to make anything¦338832? Would anyone \add ≈use\add* \add @vine wood\add* \add even\add* to make something to hang a mug on?
\v 4 If it's \add ≈used as firewood\add*, and if the fire burns both¦338849 ends, and even the middle¦338853, is it good \add wood, or indeed good\add* for anything¦338856?
\v 5 \add ≈Originally,\add* \add @the vine wood\add* couldn't \add be used to\add* make anything, so surely, when the fire's¦338867 burnt it, it still can't¦338861 do anything useful.
\p
\v 6 Therefore the master¦338878 Yahweh¦338878 says¦338877 this: ‘Unlike the trees¦338884 in the forests¦338885, I've¦338892 given the vine¦338883 as fuel for fires. I'll act in the same way toward Yerushalem's¦338896 inhabitants¦338895,
\v 7 and¦338898 I'll¦338898 \add ≈start to take action\add* against them. Even if they get out of the fire, the fire will still consume¦338906 them, so you \add people\add* will know that I am Yahweh¦338911, when I \add ≈take action\add* against them.
\v 8 Then¦338918 I'll¦338918 make¦338918 the land into an abandoned wasteland because¦338923 they¦338924 \add ≈chose to worship other gods\add*. That's the master¦338927 Yahweh's¦338928 declaration.”
\c 16
\s1 Unfaithful Yerushalem's vile practices
\rem /s1 Jerusalem—an Unfaithful Wife; Jerusalem the Unfaithful; An Allegory of Unfaithful Jerusalem; God's Faithless Bride
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦338934 \add ≈gave\add* me \add another\add* message¦338932:
\v 2 “Humanity's child, inform Yerushalem¦338944 about \add ≈their detestable behaviour\add*,
\v 3 and declare that the master¦338953 Yahweh¦338953 says¦338952 this to Yerushalem¦338955: Your beginning and your birth¦338957 took place in the land¦338958 of Canaan, your father¦338960 was an Amorite¦338961, and your mother¦338962 was a Hittite¦338963.\f + \fr 16:3 \ft A bunch of insults to the proud Israelis.\f*
\v 4 \add ≈When¦338965 you were born\add*, your mother didn't¦338969 cut¦338971 your cord¦338972, nor did she clean¦338977 you with water¦338973 or rub you down with salt, or wrap cloth around you.
\v 5 No \add ≈one cared enough\add* about you to do any of these¦338993 things for you—to be compassionate toward you. Your¦339002 life¦339002 \add ≈was despised\add* \add and\add* you were thrown¦338996 out into the open field¦339000 on¦339001 the \add very\add* day¦339003 that you were born.
\p
\v 6 But¦339007 I went past, and¦339007 I saw you, \add Yerushalem,\add* writhing in your own blood, so I said to you \add as you lay there\add* in your blood, “Live!”\f + \fr 16:6 \ft The last part of the verse is repeated in the Hebrew.\f*
\v 7 I made¦339024 you grow like a plant¦339022 in¦339028 the countryside¦339023. You grew up and became tall, and you became the \add ≈most precious\add* jewel¦339028. Your breasts¦339030 became firm, and your hair¦339032 grew thick, even though you'd been naked¦339035 and bare.
\p
\v 8 I went¦339052 past again and saw you. Wow, the time of love came for you, so I spread¦339045 my robe out over you and covered¦339048 your¦339042 nakedness¦339049. Then¦339038 I \add ≈made a promise\add* to you and brought you into a contract and you became¦339058 mine. That's the master¦339056 Yahweh's¦339057 declaration.
\p
\v 9 I washed¦339063 you, \add Yerushalem,\add* with¦339062 water¦339062, and rinsed your blood¦339064 off you, and I \add ≈put lotion on¦339062 your skin\add*.
\v 10 Then¦339069 I dressed you in embroidered clothes¦339069 and¦339069 put leather¦339072 sandals¦339071 on¦339074 your feet. I wrapped¦339073 you in fine linen¦339074, then¦339069 covered¦339075 you with¦339074 silk.
\v 11 Next I adorned¦339078 you¦339078 with jewellery, and I put bracelets¦339081 on your hands¦339084 and a chain¦339085 around your neck.
\v 12 I put a ring in your nose¦339094 and earrings¦339095 in your ears¦339098, and a beautiful¦339100 crown¦339099 on¦339101 your head¦339101.
\v 13 So¦339103 you were adorned¦339103 with¦339117 gold¦339104 and silver¦339105, and you were dressed in¦339117 fine linen¦339107, silk, and embroidered¦339110 clothes¦339106. You ate¦339114 \add good food made from\add* fine flour¦339111, honey¦339112, and oil¦339113, and you were very beautiful¦339116, and you became a queen¦339120.
\v 14 Your \add ≈reputation¦339124\add*, \add Yerushalem,\add* \add ≈spread\add* among¦339125 the nations¦339125 because of your beauty¦339126, because it was perfect¦339129 in¦339125 the majesty I'd given you. That's the master¦339137 Yahweh's¦339138 declaration.
\p
\v 15 But¦339140 \add Yerushalem,\add* you trusted¦339140 in¦339141 your own beauty, and you acted¦339142 like a prostitute because of your reputation¦339145. You \add ≈flirted with¦339141 everyone¦339152 going past, and prostituted yourself\add*, so that your beauty became theirs.
\v 16 Then¦339159 you took¦339159 your¦339160 clothes¦339160 and made¦339161 \add ≈hilltop¦339164 shrines¦339164\add* for yourself with them, decorated in various colours, and there you acted¦339166 like a prostitute¦339166. This shouldn't¦339168 have happened, nor should such a thing exist.
\v 17 You took¦339173 the fine gold¦339176 and silver¦339177 jewellery that¦339178 I gave¦339179 you, and you made¦339181 male¦339185 sculptures for yourselves, and you \add ≈behaved with¦339188 them like a prostitute¦339186 would\add*.
\v 18 You took¦339190 your¦339194 embroidered¦339194 garments and covered¦339195 \add @those idols\add*, and you¦339198 \add ≈offered\add* my oils and perfumes to them.
\v 19 The \add high-quality\add* bread¦339202 that¦339203 I gave¦339205 you (made with fine flour¦339207, oil¦339208, and honey¦339209), you placed \add ≈in front of\add* them to be a fragrant aroma¦339213, \add ≈and indeed it¦339211 was\add*. That's the master¦339217 Yahweh's¦339218 declaration.
\p
\v 20 Then¦339220 you took¦339220 your sons¦339223 and daughters¦339226 that you bore for me, and you sacrificed¦339230 them to \add @those idols\add* to be devoured¦339232 as food. Are your acts of prostitution¦339234 a small¦339233 matter?
\v 21 You slaughtered¦339237 my children¦339240 for the idols and¦339241 made¦339242 them pass¦339242 through¦339242 the fire.
\v 22 In all your \add ≈evil goings on¦339258\add* and your acts of prostitution¦339250, you \add ≈never thought back to\add* the days¦339256 \add ≈when you were young\add*, when you were naked¦339259 and bare as you thrashed about¦339261 in¦339258 your \add own\add* blood¦339262.
\rem /s1 Jerusalem's Life as a Prostitute
\v 23 After all your¦339269 wickedness¦339269, \add ≈you won't end well\add*. That's the master¦339274 Yahweh's¦339275 declaration.
\s1 The anger of God on Yerushalem
\p
\v 24 You made¦339282 yourself a mound¦339280 and¦339282 built¦339277 a raised shrine in every public square.
\v 25 You built¦339296 your raised platform at the top of every¦339292 street and made¦339298 your beauty¦339301 a disgrace, and you spread¦339302 your legs for anyone¦339308 who passed¦339308 by, and you multiplied your acts of prostitution¦339298.
\v 26 You've acted¦339315 like a prostitute with your lusty neighbours¦339321 the Egyptians, and¦339315 you committed many more acts of prostitution, provoking¦339328 me to anger¦339328.
\p
\v 27 Listen, I'll hit you with¦339337 my hand and¦339330 cut off your food \add supply\add*. I'll hand your life over to your enemies¦339338, the daughters¦339339 of the Philistines¦339340, who were ashamed¦339341 of your obscene behaviour.
\p
\v 28 You've acted like a prostitute with the Assyrians because¦339350 you couldn't be satisfied. You acted like a prostitute and¦339345 still you weren't satisfied.
\v 29 \add ≈So¦339357\add* you performed many more acts of prostitution¦339360 in¦339368 \add Babylonia\add* (the \add ≈country\add* of the Chaldean¦339365 merchants¦339364), and¦339357 even that didn't¦339369 satisfy¦339370 you.
\v 30 Your heart¦339374 is so sick that you would do things like that—things that only a shameless prostitute¦339387 would do. That's the master¦339376 Yahweh's¦339377 declaration.
\p
\v 31 You made¦339397 your mounds¦339391 at the top of every street and built¦339390 your tall shrines in every public square, \add ≈yet\add* you weren't like a prostitute¦339406, \add ≈in the sense that\add* you scoffed at taking payment.
\v 32 You adulterous¦339411 woman¦339410, you \add ≈prefer\add* strangers¦339417 \add ≈over\add* your husband¦339413.
\v 33 \add It's normal for\add* \add ≈clients to pay\add* the prostitute, but¦339425 you \add do the opposite\add*: you give¦339422 your wages to all your lovers¦339432 and bribe¦339433 them to come¦339435 to you from all around¦339437 for your acts of prostitution.
\v 34 \add ≈Yes,\add* there's a difference between you and¦339440 other women¦339446. No one offers payment¦339453 for you to act as a prostitute¦339450. You're the very opposite¦339459—you \add ≈paid\add* them \add ≈but¦339440\add* nothing was given¦339455 to you.
\s1 The punishment of God of Yerushalem
\rem /s1 Judgment on Jerusalem's Prostitution; God's Judgment on Jerusalem
\p
\v 35 Therefore, \add Yerushalem\add*, you prostitute¦339462, listen¦339463 to Yahweh's¦339466 message¦339464.
\v 36 The master¦339472 Yahweh¦339472 says¦339471 this: ‘Because you've poured¦339475 out your lust and uncovered¦339477 your nakedness¦339478 through your acts of prostitution¦339479 with your lovers¦339482 and with all your detestable¦339487 idols¦339486, and because¦339474 you gave¦339491 them your children's¦339489 blood¦339488,
\v 37 then listen: I'll gather all your lovers¦339501 that you've met, \add ≈including¦339505 the ones\add* you loved¦339509 and the ones you hated¦339514—I'll gather them against¦339517 you on every side. I'll uncover¦339519 your nakedness for them so they see all your nakedness.
\v 38 Then¦339529 I'll punish you for your adultery¦339531 and the shedding of blood, and I'll bring¦339534 on you the bloodshed of my anger and passion.
\v 39 I'll¦339539 \add ≈allow them to conquer you\add* so they'll \add ≈tear apart\add* your mounds¦339543 and break¦339544 down your tall¦339545 shrines¦339545, and they'll strip¦339546 your clothes¦339548 off you and take¦339549 all your jewellery—leaving you naked¦339553 and bare.
\p
\v 40 Then¦339556 they'll bring¦339556 a crowd up against¦339557 you and \add ≈throw heavy stones¦339561 at¦339561 you\add*, and they'll cut¦339562 you apart with¦339561 their¦339563 swords¦339563.
\v 41 They'll burn¦339565 down your houses¦339566 and \add ≈punish you in several ways\add* in the sight¦339572 of many women¦339573, because I'll¦339575 put a stop to your prostitution¦339576, and you'll no longer pay your lovers.
\v 42 Then¦339585 I'll calm my rage¦339586 against¦339594 you. My anger¦339586 will leave you, because I'll be satisfied¦339585 and¦339585 won't¦339592 be angry¦339593 \add at you\add* any longer.
\p
\v 43 Because¦339596 you didn't¦339598 call to mind your younger days¦339604, and made me shake with¦339618 anger because of all those things, therefore¦339615, listen: I myself will bring the punishment for what you've done down onto your own head¦339618. That's the master¦339621 Yahweh's¦339622 declaration.
\s1 Ke what the mother like just the child woman
\p Haven't you added prostitution to all your other detestable practices?
\rem /s1 Like Mother, Like Daughter
\v 44 Listen, everyone¦339635 who speaks¦339639 proverbs¦339637 about¦339638 you¦339638 will say¦339640, “Like mother¦339641, like daughter¦339642.”
\v 45 You are the daughter¦339644 of your mother, who detested her husband and her children, and you are the sister of your sisters, who detested their husbands and their children. Your¦339646 mother was a Hittite¦339659, and your father¦339660 was an Amorite¦339661.
\p
\v 46 Your¦339671 older¦339664 sister was Shomron¦339665 \add (Samaria¦339665)\add*, and her daughters were the ones living in the north¦339671, while your¦339671 younger¦339673 sister was the one living south¦339676 of you, that is, Sodom¦339677 and her daughters.
\v 47 \add ≈Not only did you follow\add* their customs and copy their behaviour¦339688 and practices, but¦339680 in¦339681 \add ≈everything you did\add*, you've been \em worse\em* than they were.
\p
\v 48 This is the master¦339698 Yahweh's¦339699 declaration: As I live, your sister¦339704 Sodom¦339703 and her daughters didn't do as much evil as you and your daughters have done.
\v 49 Listen, your¦339718 sister¦339718 Sodom's¦339717 sin was that she¦339733 was arrogant in her¦339727 leisure, careless and unconcerned about anything. She didn't¦339732 \add ≈assist\add* the poor and needy¦339731 people.
\v 50 She was arrogant and¦339735 performed disgusting actions \add ≈in front of\add* me, so I took them away, just as you've seen.
\p
\v 51 As for Shomron¦339745, they didn't¦339748 commit even half of your sins¦339747. No, you've done¦339764 many more disgusting things than they did, and you've shown that¦339763 your sisters¦339758 were better than you, because of all the disgusting things you do.
\v 52 Also how you display your own shame—you've¦339774 shown that¦339777 your sisters were better than you by the sins¦339776 you committed in¦339776 all those disgusting ways. Your sisters now seem better than you.
\rem /s1 Sodom and Samaria Will Be Restored
\p
\v 53 From their¦339795 captivity, I'll¦339792 restore¦339792 the fortunes of Sodom¦339800 and her daughters, and of Shomron¦339806 and her daughters, and your fortunes \add ≈will be similar\add*,\f + \fr 16:53 \ft i.e., to go into captivity, but then after a time, to be restored.\f*
\v 54 so that you'll display your¦339815 shame. You'll be humiliated¦339816 because of everything you've¦339820 done¦339820, and in¦339821 that way you'll be a consolation¦339821 to \add @Sodom and Shomron\add*.
\v 55 Your sister¦339824 Sodom¦339825 and her daughters will be restored to their former condition, and Shomron¦339829 and her daughters will be restored \add ≈similarly\add*. Then¦339824 you and your daughters will be restored to your former condition.
\v 56 \add ≈You never even mentioned¦339842 your sister¦339841 Sodom¦339840 in¦339843 the period when you were proud\add*,
\v 57 before¦339847 your wickedness¦339849 was revealed. But¦339856 now you're an object of scorn to the daughters of Aram¦339855 \add (Syria¦339855)\add* and to all the daughters of the Philistines¦339860 around her¦339858. People all around despise¦339861 you.
\v 58 You'll display your shame and your disgusting actions. That's Yahweh's¦339874 declaration.
\s1 The agreement without ending
\rem /s1 An Everlasting Covenant; A Covenant That Lasts Forever
\p
\v 59 The¦339881 master¦339880 Yahweh¦339880 says¦339879 this: ‘I'll¦339882 deal with you as you deserve—you who've despised¦339889 your oath by breaking¦339891 \add &our\add* agreement¦339892.
\v 60 But¦339894 I myself will call to mind my agreement with you that was made \add ≈when you were younger\add*, and¦339894 I'll¦339894 establish¦339902 a never-ending agreement with you.
\v 61 Then¦339907 you'll call to mind your behaviour and be ashamed¦339911 when you \add ≈adopt\add* your older¦339916 and younger¦339920 sisters¦339915. I'll¦339922 give¦339922 them to you as daughters¦339925, but¦339907 not because of your agreement¦339927.
\v 62 I myself will establish¦339929 my agreement¦339933 with you, and¦339935 you'll know¦339935 that I am Yahweh¦339939,
\v 63 so that you'll call everything to mind and be ashamed¦339943. Then you'll no longer open your mouth¦339950 to speak, because of your shame, when I've forgiven¦339953 you for everything you've¦339959 done¦339959. That's the master¦339961 Yahweh's¦339962 declaration.’ ”
\c 17
\s1 The two eagles and the vine
\rem /s1 A Story of Two Eagles; The Two Eagles and the Vine; Two Eagles and a Vine; The Parable of the Eagles and the Vine
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦339968 \add ≈gave\add* me \add another\add* message¦339966:
\v 2 “Humanity's¦339982 child, present a riddle and¦339977 tell¦339977 a parable¦339978 to the \add ≈Israeli¦339981 people\add*.
\v 3 Tell \add >them\add*, ‘The master¦339989 Yahweh¦339989 says¦339987 this: ‘A large eagle¦339991, with large wings¦339994 full of multi-coloured feathers¦339996, and long¦339995 pinions, went¦340003 to Lebanon¦340006 and grabbed hold of the top of a cedar¦340011 tree.
\v 4 He broke off the top shoot¦340015 of \add @the tree\add* and took it to Canaan \add where he\add* placed¦340024 it in¦340022 a city¦340022 \add full\add* of merchants¦340021.
\v 5 He \add ≈also\add* took¦340026 some of the land's seed and¦340026 planted it in¦340030 fertile soil, \add ≈beside a large body of water¦340036 where\add* a willow¦340038 \add might grow\add*.
\v 6 Then¦340041 \add @the seed\add* sprouted¦340041 and became a spreading vine low to the ground. Its branches turned¦340047 toward him, and its roots¦340050 grew \add ≈down below\add*, so it became a vine and produced¦340055 branches and sent out shoots¦340056.
\p
\v 7 \add ≈But¦340060\add* there was another large eagle with large wings¦340066 and many feathers. Oh¦340070 wow, that vine¦340071 turned its roots¦340074 toward this eagle, and it spread out its branches¦340076 toward the eagle from the place it had been planted¦340083 so it might get watered¦340080.
\v 8 It had been planted¦340094 in good¦340088 soil beside a large body of water¦340091 so it would grow branches¦340096 and produce¦340098 fruit¦340098, to become a magnificent vine¦340100.’
\p
\v 9 \add ≈Ask\add* \add the people\add*: ‘The master¦340107 Yahweh¦340107 wants to know if it'll prosper¦340109. Won't it be uprooted and stripped¦340119 of its fruit¦340117 so that it withers¦340120, and all its fresh¦340123 growth¦340124 will dry out? \add ≈You wouldn't have to be very strong or get lots of people to help\add* to pull it out by its roots.
\v 10 So¦340137 listen. After it had been planted¦340138, would it thrive¦340139? Wouldn't it wither up when the eastern¦340144 wind¦340143 touches¦340141 it? \add Yes,\add* it would wither right up in¦340142 the garden plot where¦340150 it sprouted.’ ”
\s1 The vine part of the parable explained
\rem /s1 The Riddle Explained; The Parable Is Explained
\p
\v 11 Then Yahweh¦340157 \add ≈gave\add* me \add another\add* message¦340155:
\v 12 “\add ≈Ask\add* those rebellious¦340165 \add ≈people\add*, ‘Don't¦340166 you know what those things mean? Listen, the king of Babylon came to Yerushalem¦340178 and captured its king and its princes¦340185 and took them with him to Babylon.\x + \xo 17:12-15: \xt 2Ki 24:15-20; 2Ch 36:10.\x*
\v 13 Then he took \add a member\add* of the royal¦340193 family¦340192, made¦340194 an agreement¦340196 with¦340199 him—\add ≈forcing him to make various commitments\add*. Then he took away the \add ≈country's\add* \add former\add* powerful people,
\v 14 so the kingdom¦340207 would remain \add ≈subjected and not be able to become powerful again\add*. \add However,\add* by keeping the agreement¦340214, the \add ≈country\add* would \add at least\add* survive.
\v 15 But¦340217 the king of Yerushalem rebelled¦340217 against him by sending¦340220 his ambassadors¦340221 to Egypt¦340222 \add (Heb. Mitsrayim)\add* to acquire horses¦340226 and¦340217 an army. Will he succeed¦340230? Will the one doing these¦340233 things escape? If he breaks¦340234 the agreement¦340235, will he \add ≈survive\add*?
\v 16 This is the master¦340242 Yahweh's¦340243 declaration: As I live, he'll definitely die in the land of the king who made him king, the king whose promises he despised¦340252, and whose agreement¦340260 he broke¦340257. He'll die in the middle of Babylon¦340264.
\v 17 \add Egypt's\add* Far-oh \add (Pharaoh¦340274)\add* with¦340268 his mighty army and huge¦340269 horde¦340270 won't¦340267 help him¦340273 in¦340268 battle¦340275, when ramps are constructed and siege¦340279 walls are built¦340278 up to cut¦340280 off many lives¦340281,
\v 18 because the king despised¦340284 his promise by breaking¦340286 the agreement¦340287. Wow, he reached out to make a promise, and¦340284 yet \add afterwards\add* he did¦340294 all those things. He won't¦340295 escape¦340296.
\v 19 Therefore the master¦340303 Yahweh¦340303 says¦340302 this: ‘As I live, wasn't it my promise that he despised¦340313 and my agreement¦340314 that he broke¦340316? \add ≈Therefore\add* I'll¦340317 \add ≈cause him to be punished for what he did\add*.
\v 20 I'll spread¦340320 my net¦340322 out over him, and he'll be caught¦340323 in¦340324 my trap, and I'll take him to Babylon¦340326 and handle his judgement¦340327 there¦340329 for the treason he committed when he betrayed me.
\v 21 All of his refugees in his armies will be killed by the sword¦340344, and¦340336 the ones who remain will be scattered¦340350 in every direction. Then¦340336 you \add people\add* will know¦340351 that I am Yahweh¦340354, because¦340352 I've¦340355 declared that that will happen.”
\s1 The tree-tip part of the parable explained
\rem /s1 God's Promise of Hope; Israel Exalted at Last
\p
\v 22 The master¦340360 Yahweh¦340360 says¦340359 this, ‘So I myself will take¦340362 away the highest part of the cedar¦340365 tree, and I'll plant it away from its¦340369 tender¦340370 branches. I'll break it off, and I myself will plant it on a very high¦340377 mountain¦340375.
\v 23 I'll¦340383 plant¦340383 it on¦340398 Yisrael's highest mountain¦340380 so it'll grow branches and produce¦340384 fruit¦340387, and it'll become a majestic¦340390 cedar¦340389 so that every winged bird¦340394 will live under¦340392 it. They'll nest in¦340398 the shade¦340398 of its branches,
\v 24 then¦340402 all the trees in the countryside¦340406 will know that I am Yahweh. I bring¦340410 down the high trees and I raise¦340414 up the low trees. I wither the watered tree and I cause the wilted tree to bloom. I am Yahweh. I've¦340425 declared that that will happen, and I will do it.’ ”
\c 18
\s1 Individual responsibility
\rem /s1 The Justice of a Righteous God; Individual Responsibility; The Soul Who Sins Will Die; Individual Retribution
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦340432 \add ≈gave\add* me \add another\add* message¦340430:
\v 2 “What do you mean, you \add people\add* who use this proverb about Yisrael¦340448? You say¦340449, ‘Fathers eat¦340451 sour grapes¦340452, \add ≈but¦340453 it's\add* the children's¦340454 teeth¦340453 that are \add ≈set on edge\add*’.
\p
\v 3 This is the master¦340461 Yahweh's¦340462 declaration: as I live, there'll \add ≈certainly no longer be any occasion for you¦340466 to use\add* this proverb in¦340471 Yisrael¦340471.
\v 4 Listen, every life belongs to me: the father's¦340480 life as well as the son's—they belong to me. The \add ≈one who disobeys\add* is the one who'll die.
\s2 The godly man
\p
\v 5 If there's a \add ≈godly¦340496\add* \add >man\add* who does what's fair and right¦340496,
\v 6 who doesn't eat at the \add ≈hilltop\add* \add shrines\add*, who doesn't \add ≈request help\add* from Yisrael's¦340513 idols¦340511, who doesn't \add ≈mess with\add* someone else's wife¦340516 or a menstruating¦340523 woman¦340522,
\v 7 who doesn't oppress¦340529 anyone¦340527, who gives back to debtors what they put up as security for loans, who doesn't \add ≈steal\add* \add but¦340527 rather\add* gives his food to the hungry¦340537 and¦340539 \add ≈gives clothes¦340542 to those without them\add*,
\v 8 who doesn't charge too much interest¦340544 if he lends \add >money\add*, and doesn't take too much profit for what he sells, who promotes true justice¦340554 \add ≈within the community\add*,
\v 9 who \add ≈follows\add* my instructions¦340561 and \add ≈faithfully¦340566 obeys\add* my regulations¦340561, that man will be \add ≈acquitted\add* \add and\add* will definitely live. That's the master¦340572 Yahweh's¦340573 declaration.\x + \xo 18:9: \xt Lev 18:5.\x*
\s3 The wayward son of the godly man
\p
\v 10 \add ≈But¦340575\add* suppose \add @that godly man\add* has a violent¦340578 son who kills and¦340581 sadly \add ≈goes against all those things above\add*,
\v 11 not \add ≈following\add* the example of his \add ≈godly\add* father, but¦340586 \add rather\add* who's eaten¦340599 at the \add ≈hilltop\add* \add shrines\add* and¦340600 \add ≈slept with someone else's\add* wife¦340602,
\v 12 who oppresses¦340608 the poor and needy¦340607, who steals and robs, who doesn't return¦340613 \add something given as\add* a pledge¦340611, who \add ≈requests help from\add* idols¦340616 and does \add ≈disgusting things\add*,
\v 13 who lends out money at too high interest¦340622, and who makes too much profit on what he sells. Should that man live? He certainly¦340635 won't¦340627! He'll definitely die¦340635, and his blood¦340637 will be on \add ≈his own head\add*.
\s3 The peace/prosperity of child righteous/honest/sensible
\p
\v 14 But¦340641 listen, suppose he has a son, and his son sees all the sins¦340649 that¦340651 his father's¦340650 committed, and though he sees them, he doesn't do those things.
\v 15 He hasn't eaten¦340662 at the \add ≈hilltop\add* \add shrines\add*, and hasn't \add ≈requested help from the Israeli¦340670 people's idols¦340668\add*, and hasn't \add ≈slept with someone else's\add* wife¦340673,
\v 16 he doesn't oppress¦340680 anyone¦340678, or \add ≈keep things given¦340689 as\add* a pledge, or \add ≈accept\add* stolen things, but¦340678 instead gives his food to the hungry¦340688 and¦340678 \add ≈gives clothes¦340693 to those without them\add*,
\v 17 he's turned¦340696 his back on¦340704 \add ≈crime\add*, and doesn't charge high interest¦340698, he \add ≈follows\add* my instructions¦340704 and \add ≈obeys\add* my regulations¦340704—he won't¦340700 die¦340708 for his father's¦340710 \add ≈evil actions\add*, but¦340699 he'll certainly¦340711 live.
\v 18 His¦340729 father¦340714, since he oppressed others by extortion¦340717 and robbed¦340719 \add ≈people\add*, and did \add ≈evil things\add* among his people—listen, he'll die¦340731 in¦340732 his sin.
\p
\v 19 \add ≈But¦340734 you people ask\add*, ‘Why doesn't the son \add also\add* have to \add pay the cost for his family's crimes\add*?’ \add Well\add* it's because the son \add ≈promotes\add* justice¦340743 and godliness and \add ≈follows\add* all my instructions¦340749. He'll definitely live.
\v 20 The one who sins is the one who'll die. The children won't \add have to\add* \add ≈be responsible for\add* their parents' sin, and the parents won't \add ≈be responsible for\add* their children's sins—the righteousness of those who act rightly will be on themselves, and the wickedness of the wicked will be on themselves.\x + \xo 18:20: \xt Deu 24:16.\x*
\s2 The person repent of sins he/his
\p
\v 21 \add ≈But¦340783\add* if the wicked¦340783 \add >person\add* turns away from all \add ≈their disobedience\add*, and \add ≈follows\add* all my instructions¦340797 and \add ≈does what's right¦340800 and fair\add*, then \add @that person\add* will certainly¦340801 live and not die¦340804.
\v 22 All \add ≈their acts of disobedience\add* won't¦340811 be called to mind against them. They'll live¦340818 by the \add ≈right¦340814 things they¦340812 do\add*.
\v 23 That's the master¦340825 Yahweh's¦340826 declaration.
\p Do I \add ≈celebrate happily\add* about the death¦340822 of wicked¦340823 \add people\add*, and¦340830 not about them turning¦340828 away from their \add evil\add* behaviour¦340829 so that they can live¦340830?
\v 24 \add ≈But¦340833\add* if a righteous person turns¦340833 away from their righteousness, and \add ≈disobeys\add* and \add ≈does disgusting things like\add* the wicked¦340843 people do, then will they live¦340845? All the \add ≈good things\add* that had been done won't¦340853 be called to mind when they betray me in their treason, so they'll die¦340864 in the sins that they committed¦340836.
\p
\v 25 \add ≈But¦340866 you people complain\add* that the master's¦340870 way isn't¦340867 correct. Please¦340875 listen¦340871, \add you\add* \add ≈Israeli¦340874 people\add*: is it my ways that aren't¦340867 correct, or is it \em your\em* ways?
\v 26 When the righteous person turns¦340884 away from their righteousness, and commits injustice and dies because of it, then \add *that person\add* will die in¦340892 the injustice that they've done¦340895.
\v 27 \add ≈But¦340899\add* when a wicked person turns¦340899 away from the wicked things they've done¦340903 and \add ≈does what's fair and what's right¦340906\add*, then \add *that person\add* will preserve¦340911 their life¦340910—
\v 28 they've \add ≈become aware of all their disobedient behaviours\add* and¦340913 turned¦340914 away from them. \add @That person\add* certainly¦340921 won't¦340923 die¦340924, \add ≈but¦340913\add* will live.
\v 29 \add ≈But¦340926 the Israeli¦340928 people insist\add*, ‘The master's¦340932 way isn't¦340929 fair!’ How is my way not fair, \add ≈you Israeli¦340928 people\add*? It's \em your\em* ways that aren't¦340929 fair.
\v 30 Therefore I'll¦340947 judge¦340947 each person among you according¦340946 to their ways¦340946, \add ≈you Israeli¦340949 people\add*. That's the master¦340952 Yahweh's¦340953 declaration.
\p \add ≈Change your direction\add* and turn away from all your \add ≈disobedient behaviours\add* so that they won't¦340959 be stumbling¦340963 blocks¦340963 of evil¦340964 for you.
\v 31 Throw¦340966 off all the \add ≈disobedient things you people have done\add*. \add ≈Work towards\add* a new heart¦340978 and a new spirit¦340980 for yourselves. Why should you die¦340983, \add ≈you Israeli¦340985 people\add*?
\v 32 I take¦340989 no pleasure¦340989 in¦340990 the death¦340990 of someone who dies¦340991. That's the master¦340993 Yahweh's¦340994 declaration, \add so\add* \add ≈turn¦340995 away from your evil behaviour\add* and live¦340996.
\c 19
\s1 A song of mourning for Yisrael's final kings
\rem /s1 A Lament for Israel's Princes; A Song of Sorrow; Israel Degraded; A Funeral Song for Israel's Kings
\p
\v 1 \add ≈Now sing a mournful song for Yisrael's leaders,\add*
\v 2 saying:
\q1 ‘Who was your mother¦341009? A lioness¦341010—she lived with a lion's son.
\q1 There among the young¦341015 lions, she reared¦341016 her¦341017 cubs.
\q1
\v 3 She's the one who raised one of her¦341021 cubs to become a young¦341022 lion—
\q1 a lion who learned¦341024 to tear apart his victims,
\q1 and¦341019 then¦341019 he devoured¦341029 people.
\q1
\v 4 Then¦341031 the nations¦341033 heard¦341031 about him.
\q1 He got caught¦341035 in¦341034 their¦341034 trap,
\q1 and¦341031 they took him to Egypt¦341041 \add (Heb. Mitsrayim)\add* with¦341034 hooks¦341037.
\q1
\v 5 \add @The mother lion\add* waited¦341045 for his return,
\q1 \add ≈but¦341043 eventually she realised¦341043 that he wasn't coming back\add*,
\q1 so she took another one of her¦341047 cubs and¦341043 made him into a young¦341051 lion.
\q1
\v 6 This young lion roamed around amongst the \add other\add* lions¦341057.
\q1 He was a young lion and¦341054 learned¦341060 to tear his victims—
\q1 he devoured¦341065 people.
\q1
\v 7 He \add ?≈seized\add* their fortresses and ruined their cities¦341069.
\q1 The land¦341072 and its¦341073 \add ≈produce\add* were abandoned
\q1 because of the sound¦341074 of his roaring¦341075.
\q1
\v 8 But¦341077 the nations¦341079 came against him from the surrounding provinces¦341081.
\q1 They spread¦341082 their nets over him—
\q1 he was caught¦341086 in¦341085 their pit.
\q1
\v 9 With hooks¦341090 \add in him\add*, they put him in a cage,
\q1 and¦341088 then¦341088 they took him to the Babylonian king¦341094.
\q1 They took him to the fortresses
\q1 so that his voice¦341102 would no longer be heard¦341101 in Yisrael's hills.
\b
\q1
\v 10 Your mother¦341110 was like a vine¦341111 planted¦341116 in¦341112 your vineyard¦341112 beside the water.
\q1 It was fruitful¦341117 and full of branches¦341118 because¦341120 \add ≈there was plenty\add* of water.
\q1
\v 11 It had strong branches that were used for \add making\add* rulers¦341131' scepters¦341130,
\q1 and it towered¦341132 above¦341134 the branches,
\q1 and its height¦341139 could be seen due to the mass of its foliage.
\q1
\v 12 \add ≈But¦341143\add* the vine was uprooted¦341143 in fury and thrown¦341146 down onto the ground¦341145,
\q1 and an eastern¦341148 wind dried¦341149 out its fruit¦341150.
\q1 Its strong¦341154 branches¦341153 were broken off and withered¦341152,
\q1 and then¦341143 burnt in a fire¦341155.
\q1
\v 13 So¦341158 now it's planted¦341159 in the wilderness¦341160—
\q1 in a land¦341161 of drought and¦341158 thirst¦341163.
\q1
\v 14 Fire went¦341165 out from its large branches and consumed¦341170 its fruit¦341169.
\q1 There's no strong branches \add left\add* on¦341174 it—no scepter¦341178 for ruling¦341179 with¦341174.’
\m That's a song for mourning, and should be sung as \add *such\add*.”
\c 20
\s1 Israeli rebellion
\rem /s1 The Rebellion of Israel; Rebellious Israel; The Lord's Will and Human Defiance; Israel's Continuing Rebellion
\p
\v 1 \add ≈Seven years\add* \add after we'd been taken to Babylon\add*, \add ≈some\add* Israeli¦341195 elders¦341195 came¦341193 to \add ≈get me to ask Yahweh¦341200 for advice for them\add*.
\v 2 Then Yahweh¦341208 \add ≈gave\add* me \add this\add* message¦341206:
\v 3 “Humanity's child, tell the Israeli¦341218 elders¦341218 that the master Yahweh says this: ‘Have you \add people\add* come to \add ≈get advice from me\add*? As I live, I won't \add ≈allow you to ask for my¦341232 advice\add*. That's the master Yahweh's¦341225 declaration.’
\p
\v 4 Will you judge them? Will you judge, humanity's¦341246 child? Let them know about their¦341250 ancestors' \add ≈disgusting behaviour\add*.
\v 5 Tell them that the master¦341258 Yahweh says this: ‘On the day¦341260 that I chose¦341261 Yisrael¦341262 and¦341253 made myself¦341268 known¦341268 to them in¦341262 Egypt¦341271, I raised my¦341273 hand to \add ≈make a promise\add* to Yakov's descendants¦341265. I told \add >them\add*, “I am Yahweh your god¦341278”\x + \xo 20:5-6: \xt Exo 6:2-8.\x*—
\v 6 on that day¦341280 I raised my hand¦341283 to \add ≈make a promise\add* to them that I would bring¦341285 them out of Egypt¦341287 into a land that I'd carefully selected¦341293 for them. It was flowing¦341295 with milk¦341296 and honey¦341297—it¦341299 was the most beautiful¦341298 of all the lands¦341302.
\v 7 I told them, “Let each \add ≈family\add* throw¦341309 away their Egyptian¦341311 idols¦341310, plus¦341310 \add ≈any other detestable¦341307 things¦341307 they have\add*. Don't¦341312 \add ≈defile\add* yourselves¦341314. I am Yahweh¦341316 your¦341317 god¦341317.”
\v 8 \add ≈But¦341319\add* they rebelled¦341319 against¦341321 me and¦341319 were unwilling to listen¦341324 to me. \add *They\add* didn't¦341322 throw away the detestable¦341329 things¦341329 \add ≈they had\add* or abandon¦341338 their¦341330 Egyptian idols¦341335, so I determined to pour¦341340 my fury out on¦341321 them to satisfy my rage¦341341 among them \add ≈right there\add* in¦341321 Egypt¦341336.
\v 9 I \add ≈did that¦341357 to protect my reputation¦341352\add* so it wouldn't be \add ≈tarnished\add* in¦341360 the eyes¦341355 of the nations¦341356 \add ≈where they¦341359 were staying\add*. I made¦341362 myself¦341362 \add ≈clearly\add* known¦341362 to them\f + \fr 20:9 \ft them: Probably referring to those countries, but some translations interpret it to refer to the ones being brought out.\f* by bringing¦341365 them out of Egypt¦341367.
\p
\v 10 \add ≈So¦341369\add* I¦341372 led them out of Egypt¦341371 and¦341369 took them into the wilderness¦341375.
\v 11 Then¦341377 I¦341385 gave¦341377 them my instructions¦341381 and¦341377 regulations¦341381—\add ≈anyone who follows\add* them will live¦341391.\x + \xo 20:11-13: \xt Lev 18:5.\x*
\v 12 I also \add ≈established rest days\add* as a sign¦341401 between myself and¦341403 them—for them to know¦341404 that I am Yahweh¦341407 who \add ≈declares them different from others\add*.\x + \xo 20:12: \xt Exo 31:13-17.\x*
\v 13 \add ≈But¦341410 the Israeli¦341413 people\add* rebelled¦341410 against¦341412 me in the wilderness. They \add ≈wouldn't follow my instructions¦341417\add*, and¦341410 they rejected¦341424 my regulations¦341417, \add even though\add* whoever obeys them will live. They severely¦341438 disrespected my rest days, so I said I'd pour my fury out on¦341412 them in the wilderness in order to end them.
\v 14 \add ≈But¦341443 I did that¦341450 to protect my reputation¦341445\add* so it wouldn't be \add ≈tarnished\add* in the eyes¦341448 of the nations¦341449, in whose sight¦341452 I had brought¦341451 them out \add of Egypt\add*.
\v 15 So¦341454 I myself \add ≈took action by making a promise\add* to them in¦341460 the wilderness¦341460 not to bring¦341462 them into the land that¦341467 I'd been going to give them—a land flowing¦341470 with¦341460 milk¦341471 and¦341454 honey¦341472, which¦341467 was the most beautiful¦341473 out of all the lands¦341477.\x + \xo 20:15: \xt Num 14:26-35.\x*
\v 16 I promised that because they'd rejected¦341481 my instructions¦341484 and not \add ≈followed my regulations¦341484\add*, and they disrespected my rest days, because \add ≈what they really wanted was\add* their idols¦341495.
\v 17 \add ≈But¦341499\add* I pitied them, so I didn't¦341502 \add ≈wipe them out\add* in¦341508 the wilderness¦341508.
\p
\v 18 I told their children¦341513 in¦341514 the wilderness¦341514, “Don't¦341517 \add ≈follow your¦341516 parents' habits or behaviour\add*, and¦341510 don't¦341517 defile yourselves¦341529 with¦341514 their idols¦341526.
\v 19 I am Yahweh¦341532 your¦341533 god¦341533—\add ≈follow my instructions¦341534, obey my regulations¦341534\add*,
\v 20 and keep¦341546 my rest days \add different from other days\add* so that they'll be a sign¦341548 between me and you. \add That way\add* you'll all know¦341551 that I am Yahweh¦341554 your¦341555 god¦341555.”
\p
\v 21 \add ≈However\add*, their sons and¦341557 daughters rebelled¦341557 against me. They didn't¦341562 \add ≈keep my instructions¦341561 or follow my regulations¦341561\add*, \add even though\add* whoever obeys them will live¦341577. They disrespected my rest days, so I determined to pour¦341584 my fury out on¦341559 them to satisfy my rage¦341585 against them in¦341559 the wilderness¦341590.
\v 22 \add ≈But¦341592 I didn't¦341599 proceed, for the sake of my reputation¦341598\add*, so it wouldn't be mocked by the nations¦341602 \add ≈who saw me\add* bring the Israelis out \add of Egypt\add*.
\v 23 \add ≈So I took action\add* in¦341617 the wilderness¦341617, \add promising that instead\add* I would scatter¦341618 them among the nations¦341620 and disperse¦341621 them into other countries¦341623.\x + \xo 20:23: \xt Lev 26:33.\x*
\v 24 I decided to do that since they hadn't obeyed my instructions¦341630, and since they'd rejected¦341631 my regulations¦341630 and disrespected my rest days—\add ≈they really wanted\add* their ancestors' idols¦341637.
\p
\v 25 Then¦341642 I even gave¦341645 them instructions¦341647 that weren't good¦341649, and¦341650 regulations¦341647 that they¦341652 couldn't live¦341652 by.
\v 26 I declared them to be defiled¦341655 \add ≈because of the gifts¦341657 they gave\add* (they sacrificed every¦341659 \add ≈woman's\add* firstborn¦341661 child in¦341657 the fire) so that I could fill them with¦341657 horror so they would know¦341667 that I am Yahweh¦341670.’
\rem /s1 Judgment and Restoration
\p
\v 27 Therefore, humanity's¦341681 child, speak¦341674 to the \add ≈Israeli¦341677 people\add* and¦341682 tell them that the master¦341686 Yahweh¦341686 says¦341685 this: ‘That was also how your¦341692 ancestors¦341692 blasphemed¦341690 me when they¦341690 were unfaithful¦341695 to me.
\v 28 When¦341697 I brought¦341697 them into the land that¦341701 I'd promised to give¦341706 them, then¦341697 whenever they saw¦341709 any high¦341713 hill and leafy¦341717 tree¦341716, they offered their sacrifices¦341723. They provoked¦341727 me with their offerings, and also burnt their fragrant incense there and poured¦341733 out their drink¦341737 offerings.
\v 29 Then¦341739 I \add ≈asked\add* them, “What's this high place where¦341743 you present your offerings?” so the place is called¦341748 Bamah¦341750 \add (meaning ‘High place’)\add* to this day¦341752.’
\rem /s1 Judgment and Restoration
\p
\v 30 Therefore tell the \add ≈Israeli¦341760 people\add* that the master¦341764 Yahweh¦341764 \add ≈asks\add* this: ‘Why do you \add ≈defile yourselves¦341769\add* with¦341766 your ancestors¦341767' customs? Why do you act like prostitutes¦341773, searching for disgusting things¦341771?
\v 31 To this day¦341787, when you offer up your gifts¦341776 (\add offering\add* your sons \add ≈as burnt sacrifices\add*), you defile yourselves¦341781 with¦341775 all your idols¦341784. So¦341775 why should¦341789 I let you \add ≈try to find me, you Israeli¦341791 people\add*? As I live, I won't allow you \add people\add* to \add ≈request my¦341795 help or advice\add*. That's the master¦341797 Yahweh's¦341798 declaration.
\v 32 The thought that's¦341811 forming in your¦341807 mind will never happen. You \add people\add* say, “Let's be like the other nations¦341816—like the clans¦341817 in other \add ≈countries¦341818\add* who worship wood and¦341821 stone¦341821.”
\s1 Punishment and forgiveness
\rem /s1 God Will Restore Israel; God Punishes and Forgives
\p
\v 33 This is the master¦341827 Yahweh's¦341828 declaration: As I live, I'll¦341838 certainly reign¦341838 over you \add people\add* with \add ≈strict control\add*, and with fury that'll be poured¦341837 out on¦341832 you.
\v 34 I'll bring¦341841 you out from the other \add ≈people¦341845 groups\add* and¦341841 will gather¦341846 you out of the countries¦341850 where you've been scattered¦341852. I'll do this with¦341853 \add ≈power, pouring¦341859 out fury\add*.
\v 35 Then¦341861 I'll bring¦341861 you into the wilderness¦341865 of the \add ≈people¦341866 groups\add*, and¦341861 there¦341869 I'll judge¦341867 you face to face—
\v 36 just like I judged your¦341879 ancestors¦341879 in¦341880 the Egyptian wilderness¦341880, that's how I'll¦341884 judge you¦341885 \add people\add*. That's the master¦341887 Yahweh's¦341888 declaration.
\p
\v 37 I'll cause you \add people\add* to pass¦341890 under¦341892 my staff \add to be counted\add*, and¦341894 I'll make¦341890 you obey the requirements of \add &our\add* agreement¦341897.
\v 38 I'll purge¦341899 the rebels¦341901 from among you, as well as those who revolt against¦341903 me. I'll send them out from the land where¦341905 they're staying \add as foreigners\add*, but¦341899 they won't¦341912 enter Yisrael¦341911. Then¦341899 you \add people\add* will know¦341914 that I am Yahweh¦341918.
\p
\v 39 So¦341920 to you \add ≈Israeli¦341921 people\add*, the master¦341928 Yahweh¦341928 says this: ‘Each of you should go to his own idols. Worship them if you refuse to listen¦341938 to me, but¦341920 you must¦341938 no longer desecrate my sacred¦341943 name with¦341948 your gifts¦341948 and¦341920 your idols,
\v 40 because this is the master¦341960 Yahweh's¦341961 declaration: all the \add ≈Israeli¦341957 people\add* will worship me there on¦341952 my sacred¦341983 mountain in¦341952 Yisrael¦341958. I'll¦341973 be happy to accept¦341971 your offerings¦341980 there, along with¦341952 your choice¦341979 gifts¦341980 \add ≈dedicated to me\add*.
