\p
\v 22 Therefore, Oholibah¦343531, the master¦343535 Yahweh¦343535 says¦343534 this, ‘Listen, I'll turn your¦343547 lovers¦343541 against you. I'll bring¦343549 those¦343544 that you rejected against you from every¦343551 side:
\v 23 the Babylonians and all the Chaldeans, Pekod¦343558, Shoa¦343559, and Koa¦343560, and all the Assyrians with them—strong, handsome men, governors¦343568 and commanders¦343569, all of them officers¦343571 and \add ≈famous\add* men, all of them riding on horses¦343574.
\v 24 They'll bring many people¦343583 against you with weapons¦343579, as well as chariots¦343580 and wagons¦343581. They'll \add ≈surround you with\add* \add units with\add* large shields, small shields, and helmets¦343586. I'll¦343590 get them to punish you, and they'll punish you with their¦343594 actions.
